t_id\": \"e97842848a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-21-Release-v1-Gates.md\", \"id\": \"d0ddf0dd50f07774\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3248782459202201, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.16034189417174305, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7087964, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-21-Release-v1-Gates.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e97842848a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-21-Release-v1-Gates.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-21-Release-v1-Gates.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1139, \"chunk_count\": 2, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:02:27\", \"token_count\": 635, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-24\\n\\n# Third-Party License Inventory Report\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2024\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-21 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-09; notes status through 2026-08-15)\\n\\nRetrospective report on the third-party license audit under CIPH-40.\\n\\n## Scope of the 2026-08-09 inventory\\n\\nAn audit of the dependency tree was run to catalog every third-party license in use ahead of release, flagging anything more restrictive than a permissive license.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-24\\n\\n# Third-Party License Inventory Report\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2024\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-21 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-09; notes status through 2026-08-15)\\n\\nRetrospective report on the third-party license audit under CIPH-40.\\n\\n## Finding and immediate action\\n\\nThe PDF-parsing dependency's license was flagged as a concern, and the team swapped it for a different parser library as a direct result of this inventory.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-24\\n\\n# Third-Party License Inventory Report\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2024\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-21 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-09; notes status through 2026-08-15)\\n\\nRetrospective report on the third-party license audit under CIPH-40.\\n\\n## Status as of 2026-08-15\\n\\nBecause this report is written retrospectively on 2026-08-21, it can note the later developments: the replacement parser adopted from the 08-09 finding was swapped in on 2026-08-11, then the task reopened on 2026-08-12 when that replacement turned out itself to be AGPL-licensed, which is not acceptable for the shipped dependency set. By 2026-08-15 the team was searching for an Apache- or MIT-licensed alternative; that search had not concluded as of this writing.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-24\\n\\n# Third-Party License Inventory Report\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2024\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-21 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-09; notes status through 2026-08-15)\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 24 third parti licens inventori report owner diana document key doc 2024 last updat 2026 08 21 retrospect cover 2026 08 09 note status through 2026 08 15 retrospect report on the third parti licens audit under ciph 40 scope of the 2026 08 09 inventori an audit of the depend tree wa run to catalog everi third parti licens in use ahead of releas flag anyth more restrict than a permiss licens sourc id src gdoc 24 third parti licens inventori report owner diana document key doc 2024 last updat 2026 08 21 retrospect cover 2026 08 09 note status through 2026 08 15 retrospect report on the third parti licens audit under ciph 40 find and immedi action the pdf pars depend s licens wa flag a a concern and the team swap it for a differ parser librari a a direct result of this inventori sourc id src gdoc 24 third parti licens inventori report owner diana document key doc 2024 last updat 2026 08 21 retrospect cover 2026 08 09 note status through 2026 08 15 retrospect report on the third parti licens audit under ciph 40 status a of 2026 08 15 becaus this report is written retrospect on 2026 08 21 it can note the later develop the replac parser adopt from the 08 09 find wa swap in on 2026 08 11 then the task reopen on 2026 08 12 when that replac turn out itself to be agpl licens which is not accept for the ship depend set by 2026 08 15 the team wa search for an apach or mit licens altern that search had not conclud a of this write sourc id src gdoc 24 third parti licens inventori report owner diana document key doc 2024 last updat 2026 08 21 retrospect cover 2026 08 09 note status through 2026 08 15\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e9a8a8848a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-21-License-Compliance-Review-Review.md\", \"id\": \"8e662b9dff3b4c7d\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3184868469109786, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.12427800987282661, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7716408, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-21-License-Compliance-Review-Review.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e9a8a8848a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-21-License-Compliance-Review-Review.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-21-License-Compliance-Review-Review.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1278, \"chunk_count\": 2, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:01:48\", \"token_count\": 583, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-MEET-11\\n\\n# Fireflies Transcript: Handshake Protocol Deep Dive\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-09-22\\n\\n**Participants**: Alice (PM), Bob (Backend), Charlie (Engine), Diana (QA), Evan (DevOps)\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nDiana walked the high-latency handshake timeout. The team left handshake work blocked; no timeout-bump workaround. Path still depends on the encryption workstream.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-MEET-11\\n\\n# Fireflies Transcript: Handshake Protocol Deep Dive\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-09-22\\n\\n**Participants**: Alice (PM), Bob (Backend), Charlie (Engine), Diana (QA), Evan (DevOps)\\n\\n## Transcript\\n\\n**Diana**: Handshake triage — nominal latency was fine; Bob's earlier validation held up on the local network. On a simulated high-latency link the handshake never finishes. It times out.\\n\\n**Bob**: That matches what I expected once we left the happy path. The prototype assumed round trips stay quick. High latency breaks the exchange.\\n\\n**Charlie**: Is this an encryption cost problem? AES-256 on the wire path is in the dependency chain here.\\n\\n**Bob**: It's related. The handshake still has to complete under that load, and on a slow link it doesn't. I don't have a fix that keeps the current exchange as-is.\\n\\n**Evan**: Bumping timeouts just hides it. If the link is slow enough, we still fail.\\n\\n**Diana**: I'll leave the high-latency repro in place so we can re-check when encryption or the handshake design changes.\\n\\n**Alice**: Then we leave it. Handshake work stays blocked on timeouts under high latency. It depends on the encryption path, and we're not inventing a workaround in this meeting.\\n\\n**Bob**: Agreed — no timeout bump. We'll revisit when the crypto path moves.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src meet 11 firefli transcript handshak protocol deep dive date 2026 09 22 particip alic pm bob backend charli engin diana qa evan devop summari diana walk the high latenc handshak timeout the team left handshak work block no timeout bump workaround path still depend on the encrypt workstream sourc id src meet 11 firefli transcript handshak protocol deep dive date 2026 09 22 particip alic pm bob backend charli engin diana qa evan devop transcript diana handshak triag nomin latenc wa fine bob s earlier valid held up on the local network on a simul high latenc link the handshak never finish it time out bob that match what i expect onc we left the happi path the prototyp assum round trip stay quick high latenc break the exchang charli is this an encrypt cost problem ae 256 on the wire path is in the depend chain here bob it s relat the handshak still ha to complet under that load and on a slow link it doesn t i don t have a fix that keep the current exchang ais evan bump timeout just hide it if the link is slow enough we still fail diana i ll leav the high latenc repro in place so we can re check when encrypt or the handshak design chang alic then we leav it handshak work stay block on timeout under high latenc it depend on the encrypt path and we re not invent a workaround in this meet bob agre no timeout bump we ll revisit when the crypto path move\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e940b5088a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-09-22-Handshake-Protocol-Deep-Dive.md\", \"id\": \"edcdc1df7188b1a3\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.312429999534329, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.17333824362047, \"vector_similarity\": 0.63697743, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-09-22-Handshake-Protocol-Deep-Dive.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e940b5088a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-09-22-Handshake-Protocol-Deep-Dive.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-09-22-Handshake-Protocol-Deep-Dive.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1463, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:03:18\", \"token_count\": 417, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-35\\n\\n# Crypto Sign-off: AES-256 At-Rest Encryption Pipeline\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2035\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-07\\n\\n## Sign-off Basis\\n\\nSecurity sign-off on the AES-256 at-rest pipeline was withheld until the fail-closed deletion behavior for interrupted redaction runs (T015) was confirmed Completed — an unencrypted partial output left on disk after a crash would have undermined the encryption guarantee entirely. With that dependency cleared, the sign-off proceeded against the pipeline as implemented.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-35\\n\\n# Crypto Sign-off: AES-256 At-Rest Encryption Pipeline\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2035\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-07\\n\\n## What Was Reviewed\\n\\n- AES-256-GCM authenticated encryption applied to every redacted output file before it is written to its final location.\\n\\n- Key handling confined to process memory; no plaintext key material written to disk or logs.\\n\\n- Confirmed the pipeline degrades safely (refuses to write plaintext) if key material is unavailable, consistent with the fail-closed contract from T015.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-35\\n\\n# Crypto Sign-off: AES-256 At-Rest Encryption Pipeline\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2035\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-07\\n\\n## Follow-up Noted at Sign-off\\n\\nOn machines without a hardware TPM, the volume key is still derived from a user passphrase via PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA256 at 100k iterations. This is not a blocker for the AES-256 pipeline sign-off itself, but Diana flagged it as a hardening follow-up: moving to Argon2id would meaningfully raise the cost of offline brute-force against weak passphrases on non-TPM hardware.\\n\\n*Status*: AES-256 at-rest pipeline signed off as Completed. Passphrase-derived key hardening (Argon2id) tracked separately as a pre-v1.0 hardening item, not a sign-off condition.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 35 crypto sign off ae 256 at rest encrypt pipelin owner diana document key doc 2035 last updat 2026 08 07 sign off basi secur sign off on the ae 256 at rest pipelin wa withheld until the fail close delet behavior for interrupt redact run t015 wa confirm complet an unencrypt partial output left on disk after a crash would have undermin the encrypt guarante entir with that depend clear the sign off proceed against the pipelin a implement sourc id src gdoc 35 crypto sign off ae 256 at rest encrypt pipelin owner diana document key doc 2035 last updat 2026 08 07 what wa review ae 256 gcm authent encrypt appli to everi redact output file befor it is written to it final locat key handl confin to process memori no plaintext key materi written to disk or log confirm the pipelin degrad safe refus to write plaintext if key materi is unavail consist with the fail close contract from t015 sourc id src gdoc 35 crypto sign off ae 256 at rest encrypt pipelin owner diana document key doc 2035 last updat 2026 08 07 follow up note at sign off on machin without a hardwar tpm the volum key is still deriv from a user passphras via pbkdf2 hmac sha256 at 100k iter this is not a blocker for the ae 256 pipelin sign off itself but diana flag it a a harden follow up move to argon2id would meaning rais the cost of offlin brute forc against weak passphras on non tpm hardwar status ae 256 at rest pipelin sign off a complet passphras deriv key harden argon2id track separ a a pre v1 0 harden item not a sign off condit\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e99eb05e8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-07-Local-Encryption-at-Rest-Security-Evaluation.md\", \"id\": \"3d30fbd4bb571642\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.30686717916325057, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.13817569594750082, \"vector_similarity\": 0.70048064, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-07-Local-Encryption-at-Rest-Security-Evaluation.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e99eb05e8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-07-Local-Encryption-at-Rest-Security-Evaluation.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-07-Local-Encryption-at-Rest-Security-Evaluation.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1518, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:01:57\", \"token_count\": 466, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-41\\n\\n# Slack Thread: License Parser Swap\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Thread opened**: 2026-08-11\\n\\n**Last activity**: 2026-08-15\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-11 10:16] Evan**: Finished the parser swap the audit flagged — pulled out the problem library and dropped in a replacement. Calling that step done.\\n\\n**[2026-08-11 10:18] Diana**: Nice turnaround. I'll fold it into the re-scan.\\n\\n**[2026-08-11 10:21] Charlie**: Did you check the new one's license closely, or just take the package listing at face value?\\n\\n**[2026-08-11 10:22] Evan**: Fair question — I should have looked harder before wiring it in.\\n\\n**[2026-08-15 09:54] Charlie**: Following up on this — since the replacement turned out to be AGPL, I'm searching for an Apache or MIT alternative that can do the same parsing.\\n\\n**[2026-08-15 09:56] Diana**: Any candidates yet?\\n\\n**[2026-08-15 09:58] Charlie**: A couple, but neither one covers everything the old library did. Still unresolved as of today — going to keep looking rather than force a bad fit.\\n\\n**[2026-08-15 10:22] Alice**: Let me know as soon as one of those candidates looks viable — don't want this dragging past the rest of the release work.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 41 slack thread licens parser swap channel cipherdoc thread open 2026 08 11 last activ 2026 08 15 2026 08 11 10 16 evan finish the parser swap the audit flag pull out the problem librari and drop in a replac call that step done 2026 08 11 1018 diana nice turnaround i ll fold it into the re scan 2026 08 11 10 21 charli did you check the new one s licens close or just take the packag list at face valu 2026 08 11 10 22 evan fair question i should have look harder befor wire it in 2026 08 15 09 54 charli follow up on this sinc the replac turn out to be agpl i m search for an apach or mit altern that can do the same pars 2026 08 15 09 56 diana ani candid yet 2026 08 15 09 58 charli a coupl but neither one cover everyth the old librari did still unresolv a of today go to keep look rather than forc a bad fit 2026 08 15 10 22 alic let me know a soon a one of those candid look viabl don t want this drag past the rest of the releas work\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e8f4f0468a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-11-license-parser-swap.md\", \"id\": \"2536eeff413cf064\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3056196031275738, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.1310015187536769, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7130618, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-11-license-parser-swap.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e8f4f0468a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-11-lice