{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"tl-v1","tool":"ragflow_retrieval","arguments":{"dataset_ids":["d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37"],"metadata_condition":{"logic":"and","conditions":[{"name":"path","comparison_operator":"is","value":"sources"}]},"page_size":10,"vector_similarity_weight":0.3,"similarity_threshold":0.2,"top_k":1024,"keyword":false,"question":"Sentry crash reporter telemetry opt out audit status September 2026"},"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"chunks\": [{\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-51\\n\\n# Privacy Design Note: Telemetry Opt-Out Flag Semantics\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2051\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-06\\n\\n## Opt-Out Behaviour Designed\\n\\nThe CLI and API collect anonymous usage metrics (pages processed, OCR fallback rate) to help tune the detection engine. Setting `CIPHER_TELEMETRY=0`, or the equivalent GUI toggle, is designed to immediately stop all outbound telemetry traffic to the metrics endpoint.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-51\\n\\n# Privacy Design Note: Telemetry Opt-Out Flag Semantics\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2051\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-06\\n\\n## Design-Time Issue Found and Patched: Pending-Queue Leak\\n\\nWhile designing the flag semantics, testing surfaced that the opt-out flag blocked network egress correctly, but the `TelemetryLogger` kept writing event payloads to a local SQLite queue regardless. That meant re-enabling telemetry later would flush the entire backlog accumulated during the opt-out period, including events the user believed were never being recorded. The logger was patched to a no-op backend when opted out, closing that gap before the flag semantics were finalized.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-51\\n\\n# Privacy Design Note: Telemetry Opt-Out Flag Semantics\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2051\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-06\\n\\n## Verification (Retrospective)\\n\\nA network trace on 2026-08-24 confirmed zero outbound telemetry traffic once the opt-out flag is set, closing the CLI-side verification as Completed.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-51\\n\\n# Privacy Design Note: Telemetry Opt-Out Flag Semantics\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2051\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-06\\n\\n## Remaining Limitation\\n\\nThe third-party Electron crash reporter (Sentry) has not been audited for whether it independently respects the opt-out environment variable or requires its own disable hook for minidump uploads.\\n\\n*Note*: CLI-side telemetry opt-out is verified. Full privacy compliance for air-gapped/opt-out users cannot be claimed until the Sentry crash-reporter path is audited separately.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 51 privaci design note telemetri opt out flag semant owner diana document key doc 2051 last updat 2026 09 06 opt out behaviour design the cli and api collect anonym usag metric page process ocr fallback rate to help tune the detect engin set cipher _ telemetri 0 or the equival gui toggl is design to immedi stop all outbound telemetri traffic to the metric endpoint sourc id src gdoc 51 privaci design note telemetri opt out flag semant owner diana document key doc 2051 last updat 2026 09 06 design time issu found and patch pend queue leak while design the flag semant test surfac that the opt out flag block network egress correct but the telemetrylogg kept write event payload to a local sqlite queue regardless that meant re enabl telemetri later would flush the entir backlog accumul dure the opt out period includ event the user believ were never be record the logger wa patch to a no op backend when opt out close that gap befor the flag semant were final sourc id src gdoc 51 privaci design note telemetri opt out flag semant owner diana document key doc 2051 last updat 2026 09 06 verif retrospect a network trace on 2026 08 24 confirm zero outbound telemetri traffic onc the opt out flag is set close the cli side verif a complet sourc id src gdoc 51 privaci design note telemetri opt out flag semant owner diana document key doc 2051 last updat 2026 09 06 remain limit the third parti electron crash report sentri ha not been audit for whether it independ respect the opt out environ variabl or requir it own disabl hook for minidump upload note cli side telemetri opt out is verifi full privaci complianc for air gap opt out user can not be claim until the sentri crash report path is audit separ\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e9e43bb08a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-06-Telemetry-Opt-Out-Design-and-Compliance-Check.md\", \"id\": \"c3381a6a564a6c9c\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.4027859743720754, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.23247426624582207, \"vector_similarity\": 0.80017996, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-06-Telemetry-Opt-Out-Design-and-Compliance-Check.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e9e43bb08a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-06-Telemetry-Opt-Out-Design-and-Compliance-Check.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-06-Telemetry-Opt-Out-Design-and-Compliance-Check.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1587, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:00:54\", \"token_count\": 503, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-62\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Telemetry Opt-Out Design\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-20\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-20 11:16] Diana**: Starting the design for the telemetry opt-out. Given the privacy sensitivity, I think we should go with an \\\"opt-in\\\" model instead, but Alice wants a clear \\\"opt-out\\\" toggle in the first-run wizard.\\n\\n**[2026-08-20 11:20] Alice**: The legal team says as long as it's prominent and clear what data is being sent (mostly crash logs and performance metrics), opt-out is fine for the beta.\\n\\n**[2026-08-20 11:23] Bob**: I've got the backend ready to check for a `telemetry_enabled` flag in the config. If it's false, the `Segment` client never even initializes.\\n\\n**[2026-08-20 12:38] Charlie**: Make sure we don't accidentally log any PII in the crash reports. That would defeat the whole purpose of the tool.\\n\\n**[2026-08-20 13:15] Diana**: I'm adding a redaction filter to the logger itself. Any string that looks like a path or a filename gets scrubbed before it hits the telemetry pipe.\\n\\n**[2026-08-20 13:18] Alice**: @Diana, let's make sure the GUI has a very obvious toggle in the \\\"Security\\\" tab too.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 62 slack thread telemetri opt out design channel cipherdoc date 2026 08 20 2026 08 20 11 16 diana start the design for the telemetri opt out given the privaci sensit i think we should go with an opt in model instead but alic want a clear opt out toggl in the first run wizard 2026 08 20 11 20 alic the legal team say a long a it s promin and clear what data is be sent most crash log and perform metric opt out is fine for the beta 2026 08 20 11 23 bob i ve got the backend readi to check for a telemetri _ enabl flag in the config if it s fals the segment client never even initi 2026 08 20 12 38 charli make sure we don t accident log ani pii in the crash report that would defeat the whole purpos of the tool 2026 08 20 1315 diana i m ad a redact filter to the logger itself ani string that look like a path or a filenam get scrub befor it hit the telemetri pipe 2026 08 20 13 18 alic diana let s make sure the gui ha a veri obvious toggl in the secur tab too\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e8e456a08a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-20-telemetry-opt-out-design.md\", \"id\": \"9de459d85d19b943\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.34843983979865223, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.1623713282837889, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7825997, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-20-telemetry-opt-out-design.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e8e456a08a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-20-telemetry-opt-out-design.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-20-telemetry-opt-out-design.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1149, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:04:33\", \"token_count\": 342, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-32\\n\\n# Telemetry Opt-Out Flag Semantics\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2032\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-06 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-20)\\n\\nRetrospective decision note on the opt-out flag semantics settled 2026-08-20 for CIPH-48 (Telemetry Opt-Out).\\n\\n## Decision\\n\\nThe CLI accepts an explicit `--no-telemetry` flag. When present, it must suppress every outbound telemetry call for that invocation, including startup pings and error reports — not just usage-metric events.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-32\\n\\n# Telemetry Opt-Out Flag Semantics\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2032\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-06 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-20)\\n\\nRetrospective decision note on the opt-out flag semantics settled 2026-08-20 for CIPH-48 (Telemetry Opt-Out).\\n\\n## Why \\\"explicit\\\" matters\\n\\nThe flag was deliberately specified as opt-out rather than opt-in-by-default-off, since the goal was to give privacy-sensitive users a clear, discoverable switch rather than relying on a config file most users would never find.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-32\\n\\n# Telemetry Opt-Out Flag Semantics\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2032\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-06 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-20)\\n\\nRetrospective decision note on the opt-out flag semantics settled 2026-08-20 for CIPH-48 (Telemetry Opt-Out).\\n\\n## Note\\n\\nThis record settles the flag's expected behavior. Confirming that behavior against an actual network trace was a separate verification step and is not part of this decision note.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 32 telemetri opt out flag semant owner diana document key doc 2032 last updat 2026 09 06 retrospect cover 2026 08 20 retrospect decis note on the opt out flag semant settl 2026 08 20 for ciph 48 telemetri opt out decis the cli accept an explicit no telemetri flag when present it must suppress everi outbound telemetri call for that invoc includ startup ping and error report not just usag metric event sourc id src gdoc 32 telemetri opt out flag semant owner diana document key doc 2032 last updat 2026 09 06 retrospect cover 2026 08 20 retrospect decis note on the opt out flag semant settl 2026 08 20 for ciph 48 telemetri opt out whi explicit matter the flag wa deliber specifi a opt out rather than opt in by default off sinc the goal wa to give privaci sensit user a clear discover switch rather than reli on a config file most user would never find sourc id src gdoc 32 telemetri opt out flag semant owner diana document key doc 2032 last updat 2026 09 06 retrospect cover 2026 08 20 retrospect decis note on the opt out flag semant settl 2026 08 20 for ciph 48 telemetri opt out note this record settl the flag s expect behavior confirm that behavior against an actual network trace wa a separ verif step and is not part of this decis note\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e9a043428a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-06-Telemetry-Opt-Out-Review.md\", \"id\": \"af63545a0d15b5f6\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3332881442062456, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.1423419174374937, \"vector_similarity\": 0.77882934, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-06-Telemetry-Opt-Out-Review.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e9a043428a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-06-Telemetry-Opt-Out-Review.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-06-Telemetry-Opt-Out-Review.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 947, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:01:55\", \"token_count\": 416, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-64\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Telemetry Opt-Out Verification\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-24\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-24 13:31] Diana**: Finished the network trace tests. With the flag set to `false`, there is zero outbound traffic to the telemetry endpoints.\\n\\n**[2026-08-24 13:45] Bob**: Excellent. PR #91 is merged and verified.\\n\\n**[2026-08-24 13:46] Alice**: Thanks Diana. This is a big one for our compliance audit.\\n\\n**[2026-08-24 13:49] Evan**: I've updated the Docker image to include the environment variable support.\\n\\n**[2026-08-24 13:56] Diana**: I also tested the GUI toggle. It correctly updates the config file and requires a restart to take effect, which is exactly what we wanted.\\n\\n**[2026-08-24 13:57] Alice**: Closing. Great work everyone. :lock:\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 64 slack thread telemetri opt out verif channel cipherdoc date 2026 08 24 2026 08 24 13 31 diana finish the network trace test with the flag set to fals there is zero outbound traffic to the telemetri endpoint 2026 08 24 13 45 bob excel pr 91 is merg and verifi 2026 08 24 13 46 alic thank diana this is a big one for our complianc audit 2026 08 24 13 49 evan i ve updat the docker imag to includ the environ variabl support 2026 08 24 13 56 diana i also test the gui toggl it correct updat the config file and requir a restart to take effect which is exact what we want 2026 08 24 13 57 alic close great work everyon lock\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e921a8ac8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-24-telemetry-opt-out-verify.md\", \"id\": \"b36d3a48cfe1a3ea\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.33107146220624556, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.1423419174374937, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7714404, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-24-telemetry-opt-out-verify.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e921a8ac8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-24-telemetry-opt-out-verify.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-24-telemetry-opt-out-verify.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 783, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:03:42\", \"token_count\": 249, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"# ClickUp Task: CIPH-48\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-48\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-48\\n\\n**Title**: Add a CLI flag to opt out of telemetry\\n\\n**Status**: Completed\\n\\n**Assignee**: Diana\\n\\n**Priority**: Normal\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-08-18\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nGive the CLI an explicit telemetry opt-out flag for privacy. A network trace confirmed no telemetry is sent once the opt-out flag is set.\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-48\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-48\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-48\\n\\n**Title**: Add a CLI flag to opt out of telemetry\\n\\n**Status**: Completed\\n\\n**Assignee**: Diana\\n\\n**Priority**: Normal\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-08-18\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- CLI supports an explicit opt-out flag for telemetry.\\n\\n- Network trace confirms zero outbound telemetry traffic when the flag is set.\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-48\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-48\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-48\\n\\n**Title**: Add a CLI flag to opt out of telemetry\\n\\n**Status**: Completed\\n\\n**Assignee**: Diana\\n\\n**Priority**: Normal\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-08-18\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nGive the CLI an explicit telemetry opt-out flag for privacy. A network trace confirmed no telemetry is sent once the opt-out flag is set.\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-48\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-48\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-48\\n\\n**Title**: Add a CLI flag to opt out of telemetry\\n\\n**Status**: Completed\\n\\n**Assignee**: Diana\\n\\n**Priority**: Normal\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-08-18\\n\\n## Activity History\\n\\n- **2026-08-18**: Alice - Task Create (Open)\\n\\n - *Opened the task because telemetry must support a CLI opt-out for privacy.*\\n\\n- **2026-08-24**: Diana - Telemetry Trace Confirm (Completed)\\n\\n - *Confirmed via network trace that no telemetry is sent when the opt-out flag is set.*\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"clickup task ciph 48 sourc id src cu ciph 48 task id ciph 48 titl add a cli flag to opt out of telemetri status complet assigne diana prioriti normal date creat 2026 08 18 descript give the cli an explicit telemetri opt out flag for privaci a network trace confirm no telemetri is sent onc the opt out flag is set clickup task ciph 48 sourc id src cu ciph 48 task id ciph 48 titl add a cli flag to opt out of telemetri status complet assigne diana prioriti normal date creat 2026 08 18 accept criterion cli support an explicit opt out flag for telemetri network trace confirm zero outbound telemetri traffic when the flag is set clickup task ciph 48 sourc id src cu ciph 48 task id ciph 48 titl add a cli flag to opt out of telemetri status complet assigne diana prioriti normal date creat 2026 08 18 descript give the cli an explicit telemetri opt out flag for privaci a network trace confirm no telemetri is sent onc the opt out flag is set clickup task ciph 48 sourc id src cu ciph 48 task id ciph 48 titl add a cli flag to opt out of telemetri status complet assigne diana prioriti normal date creat 2026 08 18 activ histori 2026 08 18 alic task creat open open the task becaus telemetri must support a cli opt out for privaci 2026 08 24 diana telemetri trace confirm complet confirm via network trace that no telemetri is sent when the opt out flag is set\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e96eb2508a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-48-Telemetry-Opt-Out.md\", \"id\": \"fc6205e3092871f4\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.32609531720624557, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.1423419174374937, \"vector_similarity\": 0.75485325, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-48-Telemetry-Opt-Out.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e96eb2508a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-48-Telemetry-Opt-Out.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-48-Telemetry-Opt-Out.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 826, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:02:38\", \"token_count\": 468, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-63\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Telemetry Opt-Out Flag\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-22\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-22 14:12] Bob**: The `telemetry_enabled` flag is now fully integrated into the CLI and the API. Default is set to `true` but it's easily overridden in `config.yaml`.\\n\\n**[2026-08-22 14:37] Evan**: Can we also support an environment variable like `DISABLE_TELEMETRY=1`? That would be easier for the Docker deployments.\\n\\n**[2026-08-22 14:43] Bob**: Good call. I'll add that to the `Settings` loader.\\n\\n**[2026-08-22 14:46] Diana**: I noticed that even when it's off, the app still tries to ping the update server on startup. Does that count as telemetry?\\n\\n**[2026-08-22 14:57] Alice**: Update checks are fine, that's a security requirement. But we shouldn't send any machine IDs with that request.\\n\\n**[2026-08-22 15:13] Bob**: It's a clean GET request, no headers other than the current version string.\\n\\n**[2026-08-22 15:16] Diana**: Okay, I'll verify that with a packet capture tomorrow.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 63 slack thread telemetri opt out flag channel cipherdoc date 2026 08 22 2026 08 22 14 12 bob the telemetri _ enabl flag is now fulli integr into the cli and the api default is set to true but it s easili overridden in config yaml 2026 08 22 14 37 evan can we also support an environ variabl like disabl _ telemetri 1 that would be easier for the docker deploy 2026 08 22 14 43 bob good call i ll add that to the set loader 2026 08 22 14 46 diana i notic that even when it s off the app still tri to ping the updat server on startup doe that count a telemetri 2026 08 22 14 57 alic updat check are fine that s a secur requir but we shouldn t send ani machin id with that request 2026 08 22 15 13 bob it s a clean get request no header other than the current version string 2026 08 22 15 16 diana okay i ll verifi that with a packet captur tomorrow\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e8da02048a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-22-telemetry-opt-out-flag.md\", \"id\": \"f46eea4f85621821\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3165247346138389, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.1223125065911985, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7696866, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-22-telemetry-opt-out-flag.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e8da02048a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-22-telemetry-opt-out-flag.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-22-telemetry-opt-out-flag.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1015, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:04:43\", \"token_count\": 320, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-39\\n\\n# Compatibility Audit: Windows Build Signing Gap\\n\\n**Owner**: Evan\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2039\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-02\\n\\n## Background: Path Fix Cleared Packaging\\n\\nBackslash path-handling defects that previously broke Windows builds were fixed on 2026-08-10, and a Windows build artifact was successfully produced by 2026-08-12. Packaging itself is no longer the blocker.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-39\\n\\n# Compatibility Audit: Windows Build Signing Gap\\n\\n**Owner**: Evan\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2039\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-02\\n\\n## Current Blocker: Missing Code-Signing Certificate\\n\\nThe produced build artifact is unsigned, which triggers a SmartScreen warning and Defender flagging the binary as untrusted.\\n\\n- **Impact**: Site IT policies commonly block execution of unsigned/SmartScreen-flagged binaries outright, which would prevent installation on target deployment workstations without a manual security-policy override.\\n\\n- **Root Cause**: No code-signing certificate has been procured or configured in the Windows build pipeline yet.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-39\\n\\n# Compatibility Audit: Windows Build Signing Gap\\n\\n**Owner**: Evan\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2039\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-02\\n\\n## Path to Resolution\\n\\nProcuring a code-signing certificate and wiring signing into the release build step is the only remaining item before this clears the T029 Windows compatibility gate — and, by extension, the T011 release checklist, which is holding on this exact signing gap alongside the T005 image slim-down.\\n\\n*Audit Status*: Active. Build produces successfully; signing certificate procurement is the sole open blocker.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 39 compat audit window build sign gap owner evan document key doc 2039 last updat 2026 09 02 background path fix clear packag backslash path handl defect that previous broke window build were fix on 2026 08 10 and a window build artifact wa success produc by 2026 08 12 packag itself is no longer the blocker sourc id src gdoc 39 compat audit window build sign gap owner evan document key doc 2039 last updat 2026 09 02 current blocker miss code sign certif the produc build artifact is unsign which trigger a smartscreen warn and defend flag the binari a untrust impact site it polici common block execut of unsign smartscreen flag binari outright which would prevent instal on target deploy workstat without a manual secur polici overrid root caus no code sign certif ha been procur or configur in the window build pipelin yet sourc id src gdoc 39 compat audit window build sign gap owner evan document key doc 2039 last updat 2026 09 02 path to resolut procur a code sign certif and wire sign into the releas build step is the onli remain item befor this clear the t029 window compat gate and by extens the t011 releas checklist which is hold on this exact sign gap alongsid the t005 imag slim down audit status activ build produc success sign certif procur is the sole open blocker\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e9aa652a8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-02-Windows-Compatibility-Audit-Report.md\", \"id\": \"7d9dbdfb5b6d7c2f\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2935790108176356, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.1122978011680509, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7165685, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-02-Windows-Compatibility-Audit-Report.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e9aa652a8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-02-Windows-Compatibility-Audit-Report.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-02-Windows-Compatibility-Audit-Report.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1340, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:01:48\", \"token_count\": 387, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-24\\n\\n# Third-Party License Inventory Report\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2024\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-21 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-09; notes status through 2026-08-15)\\n\\nRetrospective report on the third-party license audit under CIPH-40.\\n\\n## Scope of the 2026-08-09 inventory\\n\\nAn audit of the dependency tree was run to catalog every third-party license in use ahead of release, flagging anything more restrictive than a permissive license.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-24\\n\\n# Third-Party License Inventory Report\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2024\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-21 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-09; notes status through 2026-08-15)\\n\\nRetrospective report on the third-party license audit under CIPH-40.\\n\\n## Finding and immediate action\\n\\nThe PDF-parsing dependency's license was flagged as a concern, and the team swapped it for a different parser library as a direct result of this inventory.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-24\\n\\n# Third-Party License Inventory Report\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2024\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-21 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-09; notes status through 2026-08-15)\\n\\nRetrospective report on the third-party license audit under CIPH-40.\\n\\n## Status as of 2026-08-15\\n\\nBecause this report is written retrospectively on 2026-08-21, it can note the later developments: the replacement parser adopted from the 08-09 finding was swapped in on 2026-08-11, then the task reopened on 2026-08-12 when that replacement turned out itself to be AGPL-licensed, which is not acceptable for the shipped dependency set. By 2026-08-15 the team was searching for an Apache- or MIT-licensed alternative; that search had not concluded as of this writing.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-24\\n\\n# Third-Party License Inventory Report\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2024\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-21 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-09; notes status through 2026-08-15)\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 24 third parti licens inventori report owner diana document key doc 2024 last updat 2026 08 21 retrospect cover 2026 08 09 note status through 2026 08 15 retrospect report on the third parti licens audit un