 so we don't lose them.\\n\\n**[2026-06-30 09:01] Alice**: Team, we're falling behind on core engine work. I'm deferring the auth module to v1.1. For v1.0, the API assumes a trusted local network.\\n\\n**[2026-06-30 09:19] Diana**: Manageable if we stay local-network-only. I'll note the deferral.\\n\\n**[2026-06-30 09:21] Bob**: Fine. I'll keep the seams clean so adding auth later isn't a rewrite.\\n\\n**[2026-08-05 11:04] Bob**: Still deferred — capturing v1.1 auth requirements while we remember them: REST auth with rotation support, since v1.0 is local-network-only.\\n\\n**[2026-08-05 11:06] Diana**: Agreed. Folding that into the deferred-work notes so it survives until v1.1 planning.\\n\\n**[2026-08-20 10:11] Alice**: Rechecked release scope for v1.0 — auth stays deferred to post-v1.0.0. Trusted-network assumption still holds.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 08 slack thread api authent deferr channel cipherdoc thread open 2026 06 28 last activ 2026 08 20 2026 06 28 13 07 bob look into rest api auth for v1 0 do we need a full auth stori now or is trust local network enough for the first releas 2026 06 28 13 22 diana given the pii involv someth robust would be nice but if this is strict local network onli we might not need it for v1 0 2026 06 28 14 00 bob do a short studi either way what we d need if we keep auth in scope versus what we defer 2026 06 29 14 23 diana if we defer we should at least write down the v1 1 requir so we don t lose them 2026 06 30 09 01 alic team we re fall behind on core engin work i m defer the auth modul to v1 1 for v1 0 the api assum a trust local network 2026 06 30 09 19 diana manag if we stay local network onli i ll note the deferr 2026 06 30 09 21 bob fine i ll keep the seam clean so ad auth later isn t a rewrit 2026 08 0511 04 bob still defer captur v1 1 auth requir while we rememb them rest auth with rotat support sinc v1 0 is local network onli 2026 08 0511 06 diana agre fold that into the defer work note so it surviv until v1 1 plan 2026 08 20 10 11 alic recheck releas scope for v1 0 auth stay defer to post v1 0 0 trust network assumpt still hold\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e8f690d68a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-28-defer-auth.md\", \"id\": \"8320be9e419ec3ba\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3057760532064179, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.1333805188663113, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7080323, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-28-defer-auth.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e8f690d68a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-28-defer-auth.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-28-defer-auth.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1525, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:04:17\", \"token_count\": 479, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-07\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Blocked on Upstream PDF Library\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Thread opened**: 2026-06-26\\n\\n**Last activity**: 2026-09-10\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-06-26 09:10] Charlie**: Bad news on the offset mismatch fix. It's definitely coming from `pdfminer.six`. There's an open issue on their repo for the whitespace handling we're hitting.\\n\\n**[2026-06-26 09:57] Alice**: Any workaround? We can't stay blocked on this forever.\\n\\n**[2026-06-26 09:58] Charlie**: Leaving it blocked for now. Local patches aren't getting us a clean fix — it's too deep in the parser.\\n\\n**[2026-08-05 14:18] Charlie**: Still watching upstream — there's a PR against pdfminer.six, #992, that should cover the whitespace fix, but it hasn't merged. No movement from the maintainers.\\n\\n**[2026-08-20 15:58] Charlie**: Spent some time this week evaluating whether we fork pdfminer.six ourselves to get the fix in sooner.\\n\\n**[2026-08-20 16:01] Alice**: What's the team's read on that?\\n\\n**[2026-08-20 17:55] Charlie**: We're passing on it. Maintaining a PDF parsing fork long-term is more risk than the wait. Staying blocked on #992.\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 10:24] Charlie**: Checked again — #992 is still unmerged. No safe local path that doesn't involve owning a fork, so we're leaving the offset fix blocked pending the upstream merge.\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 10:41] Alice**: This is becoming a real risk for the v1.0 timeline.\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 10:55] Charlie**: Agreed, but I'd rather eat the delay than take on a parser fork we can't maintain.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 07 slack thread block on upstream pdf librari channel cipherdoc thread open 2026 06 26 last activ 2026 09 10 2026 06 26 09 10 charli bad news on the offset mismatch fix it s definit come from pdfminer six there s an open issu on their repo for the whitespac handl we re hit 2026 06 26 09 57 alic ani workaround we can t stay block on this forev 2026 06 26 09 58 charli leav it block for now local patch aren t get u a clean fix it s too deep in the parser 2026 08 05 14 18 charli still watch upstream there s a pr against pdfminer six 992 that should cover the whitespac fix but it hasn t merg no movement from the maintain 2026 08 20 15 58 charli spent some time this week evalu whether we fork pdfminer six ourselv to get the fix in sooner 2026 08 2016 01 alic what s the team s read on that 2026 08 2017 55 charli we re pass on it maintain a pdf pars fork long term is more risk than the wait stay block on 992 2026 09 1010 24 charli check again 992 is still unmerg no safe local path that doesn t involv own a fork so we re leav the offset fix block pend the upstream merg 2026 09 1010 41 alic this is becom a real risk for the v1 0 timelin 2026 09 1010 55 charli agre but i d rather eat the delay than take on a parser fork we can t maintain\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e92c1abc8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-26-blocked-on-upstream.md\", \"id\": \"68389a2a4ecca69d\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2924442422064179, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.1333805188663113, \"vector_similarity\": 0.66359293, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-26-blocked-on-upstream.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e92c1abc8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-26-blocked-on-upstream.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-26-blocked-on-upstream.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1522, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:03:33\", \"token_count\": 462, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"# ClickUp Task: CIPH-19\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-19\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-19\\n\\n**Title**: REST API Authentication\\n\\n**Status**: Deferred\\n\\n**Assignee**: Bob\\n\\n**Priority**: Normal\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-06-27\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nImplement authentication/authorization for the REST API (WS-02). Alice deferred this task to v1.1 since v1.0 scope is local-network-only; the deferral was later reconfirmed for the v1.0 release scope. While deferred, Bob is capturing the v1.1 REST-auth requirements so the work is ready when scope reopens.\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-19\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-19\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-19\\n\\n**Title**: REST API Authentication\\n\\n**Status**: Deferred\\n\\n**Assignee**: Bob\\n\\n**Priority**: Normal\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-06-27\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- v1.1 authentication requirements documented while the task is Deferred.\\n\\n- Task remains Deferred until v1.0 scope reopens for REST API authentication.\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-19\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-19\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-19\\n\\n**Title**: REST API Authentication\\n\\n**Status**: Deferred\\n\\n**Assignee**: Bob\\n\\n**Priority**: Normal\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-06-27\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nImplement authentication/authorization for the REST API (WS-02). Alice deferred this task to v1.1 since v1.0 scope is local-network-only; the deferral was later reconfirmed for the v1.0 release scope. While deferred, Bob is capturing the v1.1 REST-auth requirements so the work is ready when scope reopens.\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-19\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-19\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-19\\n\\n**Title**: REST API Authentication\\n\\n**Status**: Deferred\\n\\n**Assignee**: Bob\\n\\n**Priority**: Normal\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-06-27\\n\\n## Activity History\\n\\n- **2026-06-27**: Bob - Task Create (Open)\\n\\n - *Task opened to scope REST API authentication.*\\n\\n- **2026-08-05**: Bob - Capture v1.1 auth requirements while deferred (Deferred)\\n\\n - *Documented deferred v1.1 REST API authentication requirements while v1.0 scope stays local-network-only.*\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"clickup task ciph 19 sourc id src cu ciph 19 task id ciph 19 titl rest api authent status defer assigne bob prioriti normal date creat 2026 06 27 descript implement authent author for the rest api w 02 alic defer this task to v1 1 sinc v1 0 scope is local network onli the deferr wa later reconfirm for the v1 0 releas scope while defer bob is captur the v1 1 rest auth requir so the work is readi when scope reopen clickup task ciph 19 sourc id src cu ciph 19 task id ciph 19 titl rest api authent status defer assigne bob prioriti normal date creat 2026 06 27 accept criterion v1 1 authent requir document while the task is defer task remain defer until v1 0 scope reopen for rest api authent clickup task ciph 19 sourc id src cu ciph 19 task id ciph 19 titl rest api authent status defer assigne bob prioriti normal date creat 2026 06 27 descript implement authent author for the rest api w 02 alic defer this task to v1 1 sinc v1 0 scope is local network onli the deferr wa later reconfirm for the v1 0 releas scope while defer bob is captur the v1 1 rest auth requir so the work is readi when scope reopen clickup task ciph 19 sourc id src cu ciph 19 task id ciph 19 titl rest api authent status defer assigne bob prioriti normal date creat 2026 06 27 activ histori 2026 06 27 bob task creat open task open to scope rest api authent 2026 08 05 bob captur v1 1 auth requir while defer defer document defer v1 1 rest api authent requir while v1 0 scope stay local network onli\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e98c2be68a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-19-REST-API-Auth.md\", \"id\": \"161e89fffbbddd56\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2800795691592923, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.10547882737041758, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6874813, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-19-REST-API-Auth.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e98c2be68a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-19-REST-API-Auth.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-19-REST-API-Auth.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1005, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:02:11\", \"token_count\": 543, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-51\\n\\n# Privacy Design Note: Telemetry Opt-Out Flag Semantics\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2051\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-06\\n\\n## Opt-Out Behaviour Designed\\n\\nThe CLI and API collect anonymous usage metrics (pages processed, OCR fallback rate) to help tune the detection engine. Setting `CIPHER_TELEMETRY=0`, or the equivalent GUI toggle, is designed to immediately stop all outbound telemetry traffic to the metrics endpoint.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-51\\n\\n# Privacy Design Note: Telemetry Opt-Out Flag Semantics\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2051\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-06\\n\\n## Design-Time Issue Found and Patched: Pending-Queue Leak\\n\\nWhile designing the flag semantics, testing surfaced that the opt-out flag blocked network egress correctly, but the `TelemetryLogger` kept writing event payloads to a local SQLite queue regardless. That meant re-enabling telemetry later would flush the entire backlog accumulated during the opt-out period, including events the user believed were never being recorded. The logger was patched to a no-op backend when opted out, closing that gap before the flag semantics were finalized.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-51\\n\\n# Privacy Design Note: Telemetry Opt-Out Flag Semantics\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2051\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-06\\n\\n## Verification (Retrospective)\\n\\nA network trace on 2026-08-24 confirmed zero outbound telemetry traffic once the opt-out flag is set, closing the CLI-side verification as Completed.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-51\\n\\n# Privacy Design Note: Telemetry Opt-Out Flag Semantics\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2051\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-06\\n\\n## Remaining Limitation\\n\\nThe third-party Electron crash reporter (Sentry) has not been audited for whether it independently respects the opt-out environment variable or requires its own disable hook for minidump uploads.\\n\\n*Note*: CLI-side telemetry opt-out is verified. Full privacy compliance for air-gapped/opt-out users cannot be claimed until the Sentry crash-reporter path is audited separately.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 51 privaci design note telemetri opt out flag semant owner diana document key doc 2051 last updat 2026 09 06 opt out behaviour design the cli and api collect anonym usag metric page process ocr fallback rate to help tune the detect engin set cipher _ telemetri 0 or the equival gui toggl is design to immedi stop all outbound telemetri traffic to the metric endpoint sourc id src gdoc 51 privaci design note telemetri opt out flag semant owner diana document key doc 2051 last updat 2026 09 06 design time issu found and patch pend queue leak while design the flag semant test surfac that the opt out flag block network egress correct but the telemetrylogg kept write event payload to a local sqlite queue regardless that meant re enabl telemetri later would flush the entir backlog accumul dure the opt out period includ event the user believ were never be record the logger wa patch to a no op backend when opt out close that gap befor the flag semant were final sourc id src gdoc 51 privaci design note telemetri opt out flag semant owner diana document key doc 2051 last updat 2026 09 06 verif retrospect a network trace on 2026 08 24 confirm zero outbound telemetri traffic onc the opt out flag is set close the cli side verif a complet sourc id src gdoc 51 privaci design note telemetri opt out flag semant owner diana document key doc 2051 last updat 2026 09 06 remain limit the third parti electron crash report sentri ha not been audit for whether it independ respect the opt out environ variabl or requir it own disabl hook for minidump upload note cli side telemetri opt out is verifi full privaci complianc for air gap opt out user can not be claim until the sentri crash report path is audit separ\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e9e43bb08a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-06-Telemetry-Opt-Out-Design-and-Compliance-Check.md\", \"id\": \"c3381a6a564a6c9c\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2797523518970628, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.0966314955672326, \"vector_similarity\": 0.70703435, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-06-Telemetry-Opt-Out-Design-and-Compliance-Check.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e9e43bb08a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-06-Telemetry-Opt-Out-Design-and-Compliance-Check.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-06-Telemetry-Opt-Out-Design-and-Compliance-Check.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1587, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:00:54\", \"token_count\": 503, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-11\\n\\n# Compliance Audit Trail — Design Intent\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2011\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-07-08\\n\\nT016 opens today: build an audit-trail system for the redaction pipeline.\\n\\n## Intended Design\\n\\nEach processed file should produce:\\n\\n- a SHA-256 hash of the input stream, and\\n\\n- a companion JSON document recording the redaction map applied to that file.\\n\\nThe hash and the redaction map travel together so a given audit record can be tied back to a specific input.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-11\\n\\n# Compliance Audit Trail — Design Intent\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2011\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-07-08\\n\\nT016 opens today: build an audit-trail system for the redaction pipeline.\\n\\n## Status\\n\\nOpen — this captures design intent at task creation. No implementation has started.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-11\\n\\n# Compliance Audit Trail — Design Intent\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2011\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-07-08\\n\\nT016 opens today: build an audit-trail system for the redaction pipeline.\\n\\n## Next Step\\n\\nA loader refactor to support streaming input is expected to come first, ahead of wiring in hashing and audit capture.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 11 complianc audit trail design intent owner diana document key doc 2011 last updat 2026 07 08 t016 open today build an audit trail system for the redact pipelin intend design each process file should produc a sha 256 hash of the input stream and a companion json document record the redact map appli to that file the hash and the redact map travel togeth so a given audit record can be tie back to a specif input sourc id src gdoc 11 complianc audit trail design intent owner diana document key doc 2011 last updat 2026 07 08 t016 open today build an audit trail system for the redact pipelin status open this captur design intent at task creation no implement ha start sourc id src gdoc 11 complianc audit trail design intent owner diana document key doc 2011 last updat 2026 07 08 t016 open today build an audit trail system for the redact pipelin next step a loader refactor to support stream input is expect to come first ahead of wire in hash and audit captur\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e9bdc66a8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-07-08-Compliance-Audit-Trail.md\", \"id\": \"290515abfff23096\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.27951111463483336, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.08778416376404762, \"vector_similarity\": 0.726874, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-07-08-Compliance-Audit-Trail.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e9bdc66a8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-07-08-Compliance-Audit-Trail.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-07-08-Compliance-Audit-Trail.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 735, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:01:28\", \"token_count\": 309, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"# ClickUp Task: CIPH-40\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-40\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-40\\n\\n**Title**: Audit third-party licenses before release\\n\\n**Status**: Active (Reopened)\\n\\n**Assignee**: Diana\\n\\n**Priority**: High\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-08-08\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nAudit third-party licenses across the dependency tree before release. An initial audit led to swapping the PDF parser library, but the task was reopened when the replacement parser turned out to be AGPL-licensed; the team is now searching for an Apache/MIT-licensed alternative.\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-40\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-40\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-40\\n\\n**Title**: Audit third-party licenses before release\\n\\n**Status**: Active (Reopened)\\n\\n**Assignee**: Diana\\n\\n**Priority**: High\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-08-08\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- Full dependency tree is audited for license compliance.\\n\\n- No restrictive copyleft (e.g., AGPL) licenses remain in the shipped dependency set.\\n\\n- Apache/MIT-licensed PDF parser alternative is identified and adopted, resolving the reopened AGPL finding.\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-40\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-40\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-40\\n\\n**Title**: Audit third-party licenses before release\\n\\n**Status**: Active (Reopene