Task Create (Open)\\n\\n - *Opened the task because telemetry must support a CLI opt-out for privacy.*\\n\\n- **2026-08-24**: Diana - Telemetry Trace Confirm (Completed)\\n\\n - *Confirmed via network trace that no telemetry is sent when the opt-out flag is set.*\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"clickup task ciph 48 sourc id src cu ciph 48 task id ciph 48 titl add a cli flag to opt out of telemetri status complet assigne diana prioriti normal date creat 2026 08 18 descript give the cli an explicit telemetri opt out flag for privaci a network trace confirm no telemetri is sent onc the opt out flag is set clickup task ciph 48 sourc id src cu ciph 48 task id ciph 48 titl add a cli flag to opt out of telemetri status complet assigne diana prioriti normal date creat 2026 08 18 accept criterion cli support an explicit opt out flag for telemetri network trace confirm zero outbound telemetri traffic when the flag is set clickup task ciph 48 sourc id src cu ciph 48 task id ciph 48 titl add a cli flag to opt out of telemetri status complet assigne diana prioriti normal date creat 2026 08 18 descript give the cli an explicit telemetri opt out flag for privaci a network trace confirm no telemetri is sent onc the opt out flag is set clickup task ciph 48 sourc id src cu ciph 48 task id ciph 48 titl add a cli flag to opt out of telemetri status complet assigne diana prioriti normal date creat 2026 08 18 activ histori 2026 08 18 alic task creat open open the task becaus telemetri must support a cli opt out for privaci 2026 08 24 diana telemetri trace confirm complet confirm via network trace that no telemetri is sent when the opt out flag is set\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e96eb2508a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-48-Telemetry-Opt-Out.md\", \"id\": \"fc6205e3092871f4\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.26881671653100203, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.0919291379014315, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6815544, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-48-Telemetry-Opt-Out.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e96eb2508a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-48-Telemetry-Opt-Out.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-48-Telemetry-Opt-Out.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 826, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:02:38\", \"token_count\": 468, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-46\\n\\n# Design Note: Reproducible Offline Test Harness\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2046\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-06\\n\\n## Why a Harness, Not a One-Off VM\\n\\nAn earlier air-gapped check (see the manual single-VM USB-transfer test) proved the CLI *can* run offline, but it wasn't repeatable — every run required hand-configuring a disconnected machine. T027 calls for a harness that reliably and automatically denies network access on every run, so the offline claim can be re-verified continuously rather than checked once by hand.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-46\\n\\n# Design Note: Reproducible Offline Test Harness\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2046\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-06\\n\\n## Harness Design\\n\\n- Runs the batch CLI inside a dedicated Linux network namespace (`ip netns`) with no interfaces attached except loopback, rather than relying on a physically air-gapped machine.\\n\\n- A wrapper script asserts the namespace has zero routable interfaces before invoking the CLI, and fails the harness run outright — rather than silently proceeding — if any route to the outside world is detected.\\n\\n- Harness output is a pass/fail plus a captured syscall-level network-attempt log, so any code path that *tries* to reach the network, even if it degrades gracefully, is visible for follow-up.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-46\\n\\n# Design Note: Reproducible Offline Test Harness\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2046\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-06\\n\\n## Status\\n\\nDenies network access reliably and repeatably across local test runs. The harness is not yet wired into CI (it currently runs manually), and it validates network denial only — it does not itself certify the full offline batch run for compliance purposes; that sign-off is a separate step.\\n\\n*Status*: Active. Harness reliably enforces network denial; CI integration and any compliance certification are separate, not-yet-complete steps.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 46 design note reproduc offlin test har owner diana document key doc 2046 last updat 2026 08 06 whi a har not a one off vm an earlier air gap check see the manual singl vm usb transfer test prove the cli can run offlin but it wasn t repeat everi run requir hand configur a disconnect machin t027 call for a har that reliabl and automat deni network access on everi run so the offlin claim can be re verifi continu rather than check onc by hand sourc id src gdoc 46 design note reproduc offlin test har owner diana document key doc 2046 last updat 2026 08 06 har design run the batch cli insid a dedic linux network namespac ip netn with no interfac attach except loopback rather than reli on a physic air gap machin a wrapper script assert the namespac ha zero routabl interfac befor invok the cli and fail the har run outright rather than silent proceed if ani rout to the outsid world is detect har output is a pas fail plus a captur syscal level network attempt log so ani code path that tri to reach the network even if it degrad grace is visibl for follow up sourc id src gdoc 46 design note reproduc offlin test har owner diana document key doc 2046 last updat 2026 08 06 status deni network access reliabl and repeat across local test run the har is not yet wire into ci it current run manual and it valid network denial onli it doe not itself certifi the full offlin batch run for complianc purpos that sign off is a separ step status activ har reliabl enforc network denial ci integr and ani complianc certif are separ not yet complet step\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e9d8406c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-06-Air-Gapped-Mode-Harness-Design.md\", \"id\": \"26a2e97fa1bb8b9c\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.24839907653100204, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.0919291379014315, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6134956, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-06-Air-Gapped-Mode-Harness-Design.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e9d8406c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-06-Air-Gapped-Mode-Harness-Design.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-06-Air-Gapped-Mode-Harness-Design.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1618, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:01:07\", \"token_count\": 465, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-63\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Telemetry Opt-Out Flag\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-22\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-22 14:12] Bob**: The `telemetry_enabled` flag is now fully integrated into the CLI and the API. Default is set to `true` but it's easily overridden in `config.yaml`.\\n\\n**[2026-08-22 14:37] Evan**: Can we also support an environment variable like `DISABLE_TELEMETRY=1`? That would be easier for the Docker deployments.\\n\\n**[2026-08-22 14:43] Bob**: Good call. I'll add that to the `Settings` loader.\\n\\n**[2026-08-22 14:46] Diana**: I noticed that even when it's off, the app still tries to ping the update server on startup. Does that count as telemetry?\\n\\n**[2026-08-22 14:57] Alice**: Update checks are fine, that's a security requirement. But we shouldn't send any machine IDs with that request.\\n\\n**[2026-08-22 15:13] Bob**: It's a clean GET request, no headers other than the current version string.\\n\\n**[2026-08-22 15:16] Diana**: Okay, I'll verify that with a packet capture tomorrow.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 63 slack thread telemetri opt out flag channel cipherdoc date 2026 08 22 2026 08 22 14 12 bob the telemetri _ enabl flag is now fulli integr into the cli and the api default is set to true but it s easili overridden in config yaml 2026 08 22 14 37 evan can we also support an environ variabl like disabl _ telemetri 1 that would be easier for the docker deploy 2026 08 22 14 43 bob good call i ll add that to the set loader 2026 08 22 14 46 diana i notic that even when it s off the app still tri to ping the updat server on startup doe that count a telemetri 2026 08 22 14 57 alic updat check are fine that s a secur requir but we shouldn t send ani machin id with that request 2026 08 22 15 13 bob it s a clean get request no header other than the current version string 2026 08 22 15 16 diana okay i ll verifi that with a packet captur tomorrow\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e8da02048a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-22-telemetry-opt-out-flag.md\", \"id\": \"f46eea4f85621821\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2445089886396324, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.04596456948518918, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7077793, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-22-telemetry-opt-out-flag.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e8da02048a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-22-telemetry-opt-out-flag.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-22-telemetry-opt-out-flag.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1015, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:04:43\", \"token_count\": 320, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-62\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Telemetry Opt-Out Design\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-20\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-20 11:16] Diana**: Starting the design for the telemetry opt-out. Given the privacy sensitivity, I think we should go with an \\\"opt-in\\\" model instead, but Alice wants a clear \\\"opt-out\\\" toggle in the first-run wizard.\\n\\n**[2026-08-20 11:20] Alice**: The legal team says as long as it's prominent and clear what data is being sent (mostly crash logs and performance metrics), opt-out is fine for the beta.\\n\\n**[2026-08-20 11:23] Bob**: I've got the backend ready to check for a `telemetry_enabled` flag in the config. If it's false, the `Segment` client never even initializes.\\n\\n**[2026-08-20 12:38] Charlie**: Make sure we don't accidentally log any PII in the crash reports. That would defeat the whole purpose of the tool.\\n\\n**[2026-08-20 13:15] Diana**: I'm adding a redaction filter to the logger itself. Any string that looks like a path or a filename gets scrubbed before it hits the telemetry pipe.\\n\\n**[2026-08-20 13:18] Alice**: @Diana, let's make sure the GUI has a very obvious toggle in the \\\"Security\\\" tab too.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 62 slack thread telemetri opt out design channel cipherdoc date 2026 08 20 2026 08 20 11 16 diana start the design for the telemetri opt out given the privaci sensit i think we should go with an opt in model instead but alic want a clear opt out toggl in the first run wizard 2026 08 20 11 20 alic the legal team say a long a it s promin and clear what data is be sent most crash log and perform metric opt out is fine for the beta 2026 08 20 11 23 bob i ve got the backend readi to check for a telemetri _ enabl flag in the config if it s fals the segment client never even initi 2026 08 20 12 38 charli make sure we don t accident log ani pii in the crash report that would defeat the whole purpos of the tool 2026 08 20 1315 diana i m ad a redact filter to the logger itself ani string that look like a path or a filenam get scrub befor it hit the telemetri pipe 2026 08 20 13 18 alic diana let s make sure the gui ha a veri obvious toggl in the secur tab too\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e8e456a08a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-20-telemetry-opt-out-design.md\", \"id\": \"9de459d85d19b943\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.24347053863963242, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.04596456948518918, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7043178, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-20-telemetry-opt-out-design.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e8e456a08a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-20-telemetry-opt-out-design.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-20-telemetry-opt-out-design.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1149, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:04:33\", \"token_count\": 342, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-32\\n\\n# Telemetry Opt-Out Flag Semantics\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2032\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-06 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-20)\\n\\nRetrospective decision note on the opt-out flag semantics settled 2026-08-20 for CIPH-48 (Telemetry Opt-Out).\\n\\n## Decision\\n\\nThe CLI accepts an explicit `--no-telemetry` flag. When present, it must suppress every outbound telemetry call for that invocation, including startup pings and error reports — not just usage-metric events.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-32\\n\\n# Telemetry Opt-Out Flag Semantics\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2032\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-06 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-20)\\n\\nRetrospective decision note on the opt-out flag semantics settled 2026-08-20 for CIPH-48 (Telemetry Opt-Out).\\n\\n## Why \\\"explicit\\\" matters\\n\\nThe flag was deliberately specified as opt-out rather than opt-in-by-default-off, since the goal was to give privacy-sensitive users a clear, discoverable switch rather than relying on a config file most users would never find.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-32\\n\\n# Telemetry Opt-Out Flag Semantics\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2032\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-06 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-20)\\n\\nRetrospective decision note on the opt-out flag semantics settled 2026-08-20 for CIPH-48 (Telemetry Opt-Out).\\n\\n## Note\\n\\nThis record settles the flag's expected behavior. Confirming that behavior against an actual network trace was a separate verification step and is not part of this decision note.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 32 telemetri opt out flag semant owner diana document key doc 2032 last updat 2026 09 06 retrospect cover 2026 08 20 retrospect decis note on the opt out flag semant settl 2026 08 20 for ciph 48 telemetri opt out decis the cli accept an explicit no telemetri flag when present it must suppress everi outbound telemetri call for that invoc includ startup ping and error report not just usag metric event sourc id src gdoc 32 telemetri opt out flag semant owner diana document key doc 2032 last updat 2026 09 06 retrospect cover 2026 08 20 retrospect decis note on the opt out flag semant settl 2026 08 20 for ciph 48 telemetri opt out whi explicit matter the flag wa deliber specifi a opt out rather than opt in by default off sinc the goal wa to give privaci sensit user a clear discover switch rather than reli on a config file most user would never find sourc id src gdoc 32 telemetri opt out flag semant owner diana document key doc 2032 last updat 2026 09 06 retrospect cover 2026 08 20 retrospect decis note on the opt out flag semant settl 2026 08 20 for ciph 48 telemetri opt out note this record settl the flag s expect behavior confirm that behavior against an actual network trace wa a separ verif step and is not part of this decis note\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e9a043428a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-06-Telemetry-Opt-Out-Review.md\", \"id\": \"af63545a0d15b5f6\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2390181636396324, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.04596456948518918, \"vector_similarity\": 0.68947655, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-06-Telemetry-Opt-Out-Review.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e9a043428a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-06-Telemetry-Opt-Out-Review.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-06-Telemetry-Opt-Out-Review.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 947, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update