5, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-49\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Memory Leak Tracemalloc Patch\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Thread opened**: 2026-08-21\\n\\n**Last activity**: 2026-08-23\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-21 09:00] Charlie**: Switching to `tracemalloc` for the leak hunt since the usual profiler is a no-go on the offline lab box. Kicking off a fresh capture now.\\n\\n**[2026-08-21 11:05] Charlie**: Already got something. The `tracemalloc` output shows we're holding onto the full page-tree in `RedactionEngine` even after the document object is closed.\\n\\n**[2026-08-21 11:50] Bob**: That lines up with the hotspot list from earlier this week. I'll start on a patch tonight.\\n\\n**[2026-08-23 09:45] Bob**: Patch is in. Added explicit cleanup so the context manager actually releases the page-tree reference instead of just closing the file handle.\\n\\n**[2026-08-23 09:47] Diana**: Just finished a 6-hour soak test with the new build. Memory usage is flat as a pancake after the initial load. :pancake:\\n\\n**[2026-08-23 10:41] Alice**: Huge relief. Is this on top of the buffer-release fix from the large-file chunking rework, or a separate code path?\\n\\n**[2026-08-23 10:43] Bob**: Same family of fix — builds on the chunking buffer-release work. PR #84 is merged.\\n\\n**[2026-08-23 10:44] Evan**: On it.\\n\\n**[2026-08-23 10:46] Evan**: Rolling this out to the dev clusters. @Charlie thanks for the tracemalloc deep dive.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 49 slack thread memori leak tracemalloc patch channel cipherdoc thread open 2026 08 21 last activ 2026 08 23 2026 08 21 09 00 charli switch to tracemalloc for the leak hunt sinc the usual profil is a no go on the offlin lab box kick off a fresh captur now 2026 08 21 11 05 charli alreadi got someth the tracemalloc output show we re hold onto the full page tree in redactionengin even after the document object is close 2026 08 21 11 50 bob that line up with the hotspot list from earlier this week i ll start on a patch tonight 2026 08 23 09 45 bob patch is in ad explicit cleanup so the context manag actual releas the page tree refer instead of just close the file handl 2026 08 23 09 47 diana just finish a 6 hour soak test with the new build memori usag is flat a a pancak after the initi load pancak 2026 08 23 10 41 alic huge relief is this on top of the buffer releas fix from the larg file chunk rework or a separ code path 2026 08 23 10 43 bob same famili of fix build on the chunk buffer releas work pr 84 is merg 2026 08 23 10 44 evan on it 2026 08 23 10 46 evan roll this out to the dev cluster charli thank for the tracemalloc deep dive\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e8e281228a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-21-memory-leak-tracemalloc.md\", \"id\": \"824fb66730068003\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2341757286396324, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.04596456948518918, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6733351, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-21-memory-leak-tracemalloc.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e8e281228a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-21-memory-leak-tracemalloc.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-21-memory-leak-tracemalloc.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1379, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:04:34\", \"token_count\": 428, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}], \"pagination\": {\"page\": 1, \"page_size\": 10,