ocument Key**: DOC-2004\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-06-28\\n\\nTask T008 (OCR fallback for documents without a usable native text layer, WS-01) has reached a Tesseract-based proof of concept today.\\n\\n## What This Covers\\n\\nA POC path for routing documents with no usable native text layer through OCR instead, so the redaction pipeline still has text to run detection against.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-04\\n\\n# OCR Fallback — Tesseract Proof of Concept\\n\\n**Owner**: Charlie\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2004\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-06-28\\n\\nTask T008 (OCR fallback for documents without a usable native text layer, WS-01) has reached a Tesseract-based proof of concept today.\\n\\n## Status\\n\\nActive — POC only.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-04\\n\\n# OCR Fallback — Tesseract Proof of Concept\\n\\n**Owner**: Charlie\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2004\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-06-28\\n\\nTask T008 (OCR fallback for documents without a usable native text layer, WS-01) has reached a Tesseract-based proof of concept today.\\n\\n## Limitation\\n\\nThis is a proof of concept, not a production integration. Performance characteristics under real batch load and confidence-threshold behavior have not been evaluated yet.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-04\\n\\n# OCR Fallback — Tesseract Proof of Concept\\n\\n**Owner**: Charlie\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2004\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-06-28\\n\\nTask T008 (OCR fallback for documents without a usable native text layer, WS-01) has reached a Tesseract-based proof of concept today.\\n\\n## Next Step\\n\\nMove from POC toward integration with the rest of the scan pipeline; no timeline set yet.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 04 ocr fallback tesseract proof of concept owner charli document key doc 2004 last updat 2026 06 28 task t008 ocr fallback for document without a usabl nativ text layer w 01 ha reach a tesseract base proof of concept today what this cover a poc path for rout document with no usabl nativ text layer through ocr instead so the redact pipelin still ha text to run detect against sourc id src gdoc 04 ocr fallback tesseract proof of concept owner charli document key doc 2004 last updat 2026 06 28 task t008 ocr fallback for document without a usabl nativ text layer w 01 ha reach a tesseract base proof of concept today status activ poc onli sourc id src gdoc 04 ocr fallback tesseract proof of concept owner charli document key doc 2004 last updat 2026 06 28 task t008 ocr fallback for document without a usabl nativ text layer w 01 ha reach a tesseract base proof of concept today limit this is a proof of concept not a product integr perform characterist under real batch load and confid threshold behavior have not been evalu yet sourc id src gdoc 04 ocr fallback tesseract proof of concept owner charli document key doc 2004 last updat 2026 06 28 task t008 ocr fallback for document without a usabl nativ text layer w 01 ha reach a tesseract base proof of concept today next step move from poc toward integr with the rest of the scan pipelin no timelin set yet\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e9b3d77c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-06-28-OCR-Pipeline-Design.md\", \"id\": \"07db511d3baaa380\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.24799004475554548, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.042553192507922125, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7273427, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-06-28-OCR-Pipeline-Design.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e9b3d77c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-06-28-OCR-Pipeline-Design.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-06-28-OCR-Pipeline-Design.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 783, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:01:37\", \"token_count\": 427, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-46\\n\\n# Design Note: Reproducible Offline Test Harness\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2046\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-06\\n\\n## Why a Harness, Not a One-Off VM\\n\\nAn earlier air-gapped check (see the manual single-VM USB-transfer test) proved the CLI *can* run offline, but it wasn't repeatable — every run required hand-configuring a disconnected machine. T027 calls for a harness that reliably and automatically denies network access on every run, so the offline claim can be re-verified continuously rather than checked once by hand.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-46\\n\\n# Design Note: Reproducible Offline Test Harness\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2046\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-06\\n\\n## Harness Design\\n\\n- Runs the batch CLI inside a dedicated Linux network namespace (`ip netns`) with no interfaces attached except loopback, rather than relying on a physically air-gapped machine.\\n\\n- A wrapper script asserts the namespace has zero routable interfaces before invoking the CLI, and fails the harness run outright — rather than silently proceeding — if any route to the outside world is detected.\\n\\n- Harness output is a pass/fail plus a captured syscall-level network-attempt log, so any code path that *tries* to reach the network, even if it degrades gracefully, is visible for follow-up.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-46\\n\\n# Design Note: Reproducible Offline Test Harness\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2046\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-06\\n\\n## Status\\n\\nDenies network access reliably and repeatably across local test runs. The harness is not yet wired into CI (it currently runs manually), and it validates network denial only — it does not itself certify the full offline batch run for compliance purposes; that sign-off is a separate step.\\n\\n*Status*: Active. Harness reliably enforces network denial; CI integration and any compliance certification are separate, not-yet-complete steps.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 46 design note reproduc offlin test har owner diana document key doc 2046 last updat 2026 08 06 whi a har not a one off vm an earlier air gap check see the manual singl vm usb transfer test prove the cli can run offlin but it wasn t repeat everi run requir hand configur a disconnect machin t027 call for a har that reliabl and automat deni network access on everi run so the offlin claim can be re verifi continu rather than check onc by hand sourc id src gdoc 46 design note reproduc offlin test har owner diana document key doc 2046 last updat 2026 08 06 har design run the batch cli insid a dedic linux network namespac ip netn with no interfac attach except loopback rather than reli on a physic air gap machin a wrapper script assert the namespac ha zero routabl interfac befor invok the cli and fail the har run outright rather than silent proceed if ani rout to the outsid world is detect har output is a pas fail plus a captur syscal level network attempt log so ani code path that tri to reach the network even if it degrad grace is visibl for follow up sourc id src gdoc 46 design note reproduc offlin test har owner diana document key doc 2046 last updat 2026 08 06 status deni network access reliabl and repeat across local test run the har is not yet wire into ci it current run manual and it valid network denial onli it doe not itself certifi the full offlin batch run for complianc purpos that sign off is a separ step status activ har reliabl enforc network denial ci integr and ani complianc certif are separ not yet complet step\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e9d8406c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-06-Air-Gapped-Mode-Harness-Design.md\", \"id\": \"26a2e97fa1bb8b9c\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.24350020876641013, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.08510638395201446, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6130858, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-06-Air-Gapped-Mode-Harness-Design.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e9d8406c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-06-Air-Gapped-Mode-Harness-Design.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-06-Air-Gapped-Mode-Harness-Design.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1618, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:01:07\", \"token_count\": 465, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-28\\n\\n# Custom Dictionary: CSV Loader Notes\\n\\n**Owner**: Bob\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2028\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-29\\n\\n*Retrospective note: summarizes the 2026-08-12 CSV dictionary loader for T034; written up today.*\\n\\nOperators asked for org-specific redaction terms without forking the built-in pattern set. The chosen path is a user-supplied CSV dictionary that the engine can load alongside existing detection rules.\\n\\n## Loader in place\\n\\nOn 2026-08-12 Bob implemented the CSV dictionary loader so those site-specific terms can be ingested into the pipeline. That closes the “how do we get custom terms into the process” question for the loader layer.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-28\\n\\n# Custom Dictionary: CSV Loader Notes\\n\\n**Owner**: Bob\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2028\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-29\\n\\n*Retrospective note: summarizes the 2026-08-12 CSV dictionary loader for T034; written up today.*\\n\\nOperators asked for org-specific redaction terms without forking the built-in pattern set. The chosen path is a user-supplied CSV dictionary that the engine can load alongside existing detection rules.\\n\\n## What this does not cover\\n\\nMatcher wiring and a formal rule-test pass are separate follow-ons. This note does not claim that custom terms already fire correctly end-to-end—only that the loader exists and T034 was Active at the time of that implementation.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 28 custom dictionari csv loader note owner bob document key doc 2028 last updat 2026 08 29 retrospect note summar the 2026 08 12 csv dictionari loader for t034 written up today oper ask for org specif redact term without fork the built in pattern set the chosen path is a user suppli csv dictionari that the engin can load alongsid exist detect rule loader in place on 2026 08 12 bob implement the csv dictionari loader so those site specif term can be ingest into the pipelin that close the how do we get custom term into the process question for the loader layer sourc id src gdoc 28 custom dictionari csv loader note owner bob document key doc 2028 last updat 2026 08 29 retrospect note summar the 2026 08 12 csv dictionari loader for t034 written up today oper ask for org specif redact term without fork the built in pattern set the chosen path is a user suppli csv dictionari that the engin can load alongsid exist detect rule what this doe not cover matcher wire and a formal rule test pas are separ follow on this note doe not claim that custom term alreadi fire correct end to end onli that the loader exist and t034 wa activ at the time of that implement\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e9d330e08a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-29-Custom-Dictionary-Support-Review.md\", \"id\": \"57c62c37c116ee6f\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.23711612475554547, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.042553192507922125, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6910963, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-29-Custom-Dictionary-Support-Review.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e9d330e08a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-29-Custom-Dictionary-Support-Review.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-29-Custom-Dictionary-Support-Review.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 937, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:01:13\", \"token_count\": 339, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-26\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Node Sync Handshake Prototype\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-06\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-06 09:30] Bob**: Starting on the replication handshake for the zero-trust node sync. First requirement is that two nodes have to authenticate each other before either one accepts replicated entries.\\n\\n**[2026-08-06 09:37] Evan**: How's a node proving who it is right now?\\n\\n**[2026-08-06 09:38] Bob**: Each node has a registered identity it presents at connect time. If the peer doesn't recognize it, the connection gets dropped before any data moves.\\n\\n**[2026-08-06 09:49] Charlie**: Does the handshake add noticeable overhead to the redaction jobs running on the same box?\\n\\n**[2026-08-06 10:40] Bob**: Negligible so far — it's a short exchange before the sync session opens, nothing that touches the active redaction path.\\n\\n**[2026-08-06 10:41] Diana**: What's next after the prototype?\\n\\n**[2026-08-06 11:47] Bob**: Need to check it holds up under real network delay, not just on my two test nodes on the same switch. That's the next pass.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 26 slack thread node sync handshak prototyp channel cipherdoc date 2026 08 06 2026 08 06 09 30 bob start on the replic handshak for the zero trust node sync first requir is that two node have to authent each other befor either one accept replic entri 2026 08 06 09 37 evan how s a node prove who it is right now 2026 08 06 09 38 bob each node ha a regist ident it present at connect time if the peer doesn t recogn it the connect get drop befor ani data move 2026 08 06 09 49 charli doe the handshak add notic overhead to the redact job run on the same box 2026 08 06 10 40 bob neglig so far it s a short exchang befor the sync session open noth that touch the activ redact path 2026 08 06 10 41 diana what s next after the prototyp 2026 08 06 11 47 bob need to check it hold up under real network delay not just on my two test node on the same switch that s the next pas\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e8f020a28a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-06-node-sync-handshake-prototype.md\", \"id\": \"6657f131b0d26923\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2351028187664101, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.08510638395201446, \"vector_similarity\": 0.5850945, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-06-node-sync-handshake-prototype.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e8f020a28a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-06-node-sync-handshake-prototype.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-06-node-sync-handshake-prototype.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1079, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:04:24\", \"token_count\": 317, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"*Warning*: Do not report license compliance as resolved externally. The PDF-parser license category issue is still open, and OCR training-data provenance is unverified.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"warn do not report licens complianc a resolv extern the pdf parser licens categori issu is still open and ocr train data proven is unverifi\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e9d4f0568a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-21-License-Compliance-Audit-Report.md\", \"id\": \"e306dc15f298ee95\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.23330631675554547, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.042553192507922125, \"vector_similarity\": 0.67839694, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-21-License-Compliance-Audit-Report.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e9d4f0568a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-21-License-Compliance-Audit-Report.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-21-License-Compliance-Audit-Report.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1689, \"chunk_count\": 2, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:01:12\", \"token_count\": 582, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-MEET-03\\n\\n# Fireflies Transcript: OCR Progress Sync\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-07-05\\n\\n**Participants**: Alice (PM), Bob (Backend), Charlie (Engine), Diana (QA), Evan (DevOps)\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nCharlie reported the Tesseract OCR fallback is usable but still serial-and-slow on large docs. No redesign this meeting; parallelization deferred until the bottleneck is clearer.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-MEET-03\\n\\n# Fireflies Transcript: OCR Progress Sync\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-07-05\\n\\n**Participants**: Alice (PM), Bob (Backend), Charlie (Engine), Diana (QA), Evan (DevOps)\\n\\n## Transcript\\n\\n**Charlie**: OCR POC update — Tesseract is wired for pages that fail the text-layer path. On large documents it's still slow because we're going page by page in series.\\n\\n**Bob**: Is that good enough to leave in progress, or do we need a redesign now?\\n\\n**Charlie**: Leave it in progress. The POC proves the fallback path. Performance tuning can come once we know where the time actually goes — I don't want to redesign on a guess.\\n\\n**Diana**: I'll keep feeding it the low-confidence pages from the scan samples. Flag anything that looks broken, not just slow.\\n\\n**Alice**: Fine. Charlie stays on the OCR path as ongoing work. We'll revisit parallelization when we have a clearer bottleneck, not today.\\n\\n**Evan**: Nothing from my side until you need a different runtime layout for workers.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src meet 03 firefli transcript ocr progress sync date 2026 07 05 particip alic pm bob backend charli engin diana qa evan devop summari charli report the tesseract ocr fallback is usabl but still serial and slow on larg doc no redesign this meet parallel defer until the bottleneck is clearer sourc id src meet 03 firefli transcript ocr progress sync date 2026 07 05 particip alic pm bob backend charli engin diana qa evan devop transcript charli ocr poc updat tesseract is wire for page that fail the text layer path on larg document it s still slow becaus we re go page by page in seri bob is that good enough to leav in progress or do we need a redesign now charli leav it in progress the poc prof the fallback path perform tune can come onc we know where the time actual go i don t want to redesign on a guess diana i ll keep fe