 of the exported profile into a fresh instance to confirm no manual patching was required.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-43\\n\\n# Verification Note: Redaction-Profile Schema Export vs. REST API Contract\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2043\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-16\\n\\n## Result\\n\\nExport output matched the T004 contract on every field checked, and the round-tripped profile imported cleanly with no manual intervention. This closes the schema-export verification as Completed, dependent on T004's already-completed API work.\\n\\n*Status*: Completed. Schema export confirmed consistent with the T004 REST API contract.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 43 verif note redact profil schema export v rest api contract owner diana document key doc 2043 last updat 2026 08 16 what wa verifi the export redact profil schema design by bob expos via a rest endpoint wa check against the alreadi complet rest api contract t004 to confirm the export format match what the api endpoint actual accept and return no drift between the document schema and live endpoint behavior sourc id src gdoc 43 verif note redact profil schema export v rest api contract owner diana document key doc 2043 last updat 2026 08 16 method round trip a sampl profil through the export endpoint captur the emit schema and dif it structur against the rest api s contract from t004 also exercis import of the export profil into a fresh instanc to confirm no manual patch wa requir sourc id src gdoc 43 verif note redact profil schema export v rest api contract owner diana document key doc 2043 last updat 2026 08 16 result export output match the t004 contract on everi field check and the round trip profil import clean with no manual intervent this close the schema export verif a complet depend on t004 s alreadi complet api work status complet schema export confirm consist with the t004 rest api contract\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e9e7573c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-16-Redaction-Profile-Export-Verification.md\", \"id\": \"daac1b5e61ed336b\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2609774473452381, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.095238096207483, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6477026, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-16-Redaction-Profile-Export-Verification.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e9e7573c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-16-Redaction-Profile-Export-Verification.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-16-Redaction-Profile-Export-Verification.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1136, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:00:49\", \"token_count\": 361, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-03\\n\\n# Slack Thread: REST API Scaffolding and TempFile Policy\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-06-14\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-06-14 09:09] Bob**: Starting on the REST API scaffolding. Going with FastAPI for the layer. It's lightweight and the auto-generated OpenAPI docs will save us a ton of time.\\n\\n**[2026-06-14 09:39] Diana**: +1 for FastAPI. Can we ensure we have request validation schemas for the upload endpoint? We don't want malformed JSON crashing the engine.\\n\\n**[2026-06-14 09:43] Bob**: Already on it. Using Pydantic for the `RedactionRequest` model. Scaffold is up and running in the `api-scaffold` branch.\\n\\n**[2026-06-14 10:50] Bob**: Quick update on the file handling. I'm implementing a strict temp-file cleanup policy.\\n\\n**[2026-06-14 10:56] Diana**: How are we handling cleanup? If a request fails mid-stream, do we leave orphaned files on the container?\\n\\n**[2026-06-14 11:15] Bob**: No, I'm using a `try...finally` block with a context manager. Files are wiped immediately after the redaction job completes or errors out. No PII should ever persist in `/tmp`.\\n\\n**[2026-06-14 11:16] Diana**: What about memory-mapped files for larger uploads?\\n\\n**[2026-06-14 11:33] Bob**: For now, everything is streamed. We might need `mmap` later, but for the MVP, the context manager approach is safer.\\n\\n**[2026-06-14 11:47] Diana**: I'll start the security audit once you merge the policy. We need to be 100% sure about that cleanup logic.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 03 slack thread rest api scaffold and tempfil polici channel cipherdoc date 2026 06 14 2026 06 14 09 09 bob start on the rest api scaffold go with fastapi for the layer it s lightweight and the auto generat openapi doc will save u a ton of time 2026 06 14 09 39 diana 1 for fastapi can we ensur we have request valid schema for the upload endpoint we don t want malform json crash the engin 2026 06 14 09 43 bob alreadi on it use pydant for the redactionrequest model scaffold is up and run in the api scaffold branch 2026 06 14 10 50 bob quick updat on the file handl i m implement a strict temp file cleanup polici 2026 06 14 10 56 diana how are we handl cleanup if a request fail mid stream do we leav orphan file on the contain 2026 06 14 11 15 bob no i m use a tri final block with a context manag file are wipe immedi after the redact job complet or error out no pii should ever persist in tmp 2026 06 14 11 16 diana what about memori map file for larger upload 2026 06 14 11 33 bob for now everyth is stream we might need mmap later but for the mvp the context manag approach is safer 2026 06 14 11 47 diana i ll start the secur audit onc you merg the polici we need to be 100 sure about that cleanup logic\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e8f9c6b68a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-14-api-endpoint.md\", \"id\": \"69a1fcec04db9683\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2599652173452381, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.095238096207483, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6443285, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-14-api-endpoint.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e8f9c6b68a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-14-api-endpoint.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-14-api-endpoint.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1463, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:04:13\", \"token_count\": 436, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-12\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Batch Failure Strategy (Fail-Closed)\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Thread opened**: 2026-06-12\\n\\n**Last activity**: 2026-07-16\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 10:09] Bob**: For the batch fail-closed question, we need to decide what happens if the engine crashes halfway through a 1,000-file batch. Do we keep the successful ones?\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 10:26] Charlie**: Absolutely not. If we can't guarantee 100% of the batch is safe, we should fail-closed. No partial exports.\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 10:28] Bob**: Agreed. Drafting the plan now. If any worker node throws an unhandled exception, we abort the entire job and purge the output buffer.\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 10:43] Charlie**: I've added an exception hook to the core engine. It catches low-level segfaults and signals the controller to stop all active streams.\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 11:23] Bob**: Implementation complete. Added an atomic rename step at the very end — the output folder stays empty until the last file is verified.\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 12:53] Diana**: What about logs? We need to know *why* it failed.\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 13:16] Bob**: Crash report gets written to a separate `audit_log.json` before the shutdown. Captures the stack trace and the filename that triggered the fault.\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 13:17] Charlie**: Perfect. :lock:\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 13:19] Alice**: Thanks.\\n\\n**[2026-07-16 09:30] Diana**: QA pass on fail-closed is done — confirmed no output file gets written on failure and the temp files get securely deleted. Signing off before the encryption and offline work start relying on this.\\n\\n**[2026-07-16 09:31] Bob**: Calling this done.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 12 slack thread batch failur strategi fail close channel cipherdoc thread open 2026 06 12 last activ 2026 07 16 2026 06 12 10 09 bob for the batch fail close question we need to decid what happen if the engin crash halfway through a1 000 file batch do we keep the success one 2026 06 12 10 26 charli absolut not if we can t guarante 100 of the batch is safe we should fail close no partial export 2026 06 12 10 28 bob agre draft the plan now if ani worker node throw an unhandl except we abort the entir job and purg the output buffer 2026 06 12 10 43 charli i ve ad an except hook to the core engin it catch low level segfault and signal the control to stop all activ stream 2026 06 12 11 23 bob implement complet ad an atom renam step at the veri end the output folder stay empti until the last file is verifi 2026 06 12 12 53 diana what about log we need to know whi it fail 2026 06 12 13 16 bob crash report get written to a separ audit _ log json befor the shutdown captur the stack trace and the filenam that trigger the fault 2026 06 12 13 17 charli perfect lock 2026 06 12 13 19 alic thank 2026 07 16 09 30 diana qa pas on fail close is done confirm no output file get written on failur and the temp file get secur delet sign off befor the encrypt and offlin work start reli on this 2026 07 16 09 31 bob call this done\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e906ce748a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-12-batch-failures.md\", \"id\": \"1313e24c5f4d4803\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2596601893452381, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.095238096207483, \"vector_similarity\": 0.64331174, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-12-batch-failures.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e906ce748a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-12-batch-failures.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-12-batch-failures.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1616, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:04:03\", \"token_count\": 478, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-30\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Batch Worker Pool Design\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-03\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-03 11:09] Charlie**: Sketching out a worker pool model for local batch processing. It has to slot into the existing batch CLI rather than replace it.\\n\\n**[2026-08-03 11:41] Bob**: Threads or separate processes? Given how CPU-heavy the redaction pass is, threads alone probably won't buy us much.\\n\\n**[2026-08-03 11:43] Charlie**: Leaning toward processes for that reason. Still working out how workers get handed files without duplicating too much per-worker state.\\n\\n**[2026-08-03 12:19] Alice**: Does this need to wait on anything, or can it move independently of the CLI work?\\n\\n**[2026-08-03 12:36] Charlie**: It builds on top of the completed CLI, so the interface has to stay compatible, but the pool itself can be developed on its own.\\n\\n**[2026-08-03 12:37] Diana**: One thing to keep in mind — if files are processed out of order across workers, the audit log ordering needs to still make sense.\\n\\n**[2026-08-03 12:44] Charlie**: Good catch, I'll fold that into the design before I start wiring it up.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 30 slack thread batch worker pool design channel cipherdoc date 2026 08 03 2026 08 03 11 09 charli sketch out a worker pool model for local batch process it ha to slot into the exist batch cli rather than replac it 2026 08 03 11 41 bob thread or separ process given how cpu heavi the redact pas is thread alon probabl won t buy u much 2026 08 03 11 43 charli lean toward process for that reason still work out how worker get hand file without duplic too much per worker state 2026 08 03 12 19 alic doe this need to wait on anyth or can it move independ of the cli work 2026 08 03 12 36 charli it build on top of the complet cli so the interfac ha to stay compat but the pool itself can be develop on it own 2026 08 03 12 37 diana one thing to keep in mind if file are process out of order across worker the audit log order need to still make sens 2026 08 03 12 44 charli good catch i ll fold that into the design befor i start wire it up\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e8f350248a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-03-batch-worker-pool-design.md\", \"id\": \"ee28d048d2a09c6c\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.25085027534523807, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.095238096207483, \"vector_similarity\": 0.61394536, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-03-batch-worker-pool-design.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e8f350248a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-03-batch-worker-pool-design.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-03-batch-worker-pool-design.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1139, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:04:20\", \"token_count\": 331, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-11\\n\\n# Compliance Audit Trail — Design Intent\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2011\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-07-08\\n\\nT016 opens today: build an audit-trail system for the redaction pipeline.\\n\\n## Intended Design\\n\\nEach processed file should produce:\\n\\n- a SHA-256 hash of the input stream, and\\n\\n- a companion JSON document recording the redaction map applied to that file.\\n\\nThe hash and the redaction map travel together so a given audit record can be tied back to a specific input.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-11\\n\\n# Compliance Audit Trail — Design Intent\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2011\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-07-08\\n\\nT016 opens today: build an audit-trail system for the redaction pipeline.\\n\\n## Status\\n\\nOpen — this captures design intent at task creation. No implementation has started.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-11\\n\\n# Compliance Audit Trail — Design Intent\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2011\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-07-08\\n\\nT016 opens today: build an audit-trail system for the redaction pipeline.\\n\\n## Next Step\\n\\nA loader refactor to support streaming input is expected to come first, ahead of wiring in hashing and audit capture.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 11 complianc audit trail