library and dropped in a replacement. Calling that step done.\\n\\n**[2026-08-11 10:18] Diana**: Nice turnaround. I'll fold it into the re-scan.\\n\\n**[2026-08-11 10:21] Charlie**: Did you check the new one's license closely, or just take the package listing at face value?\\n\\n**[2026-08-11 10:22] Evan**: Fair question — I should have looked harder before wiring it in.\\n\\n**[2026-08-15 09:54] Charlie**: Following up on this — since the replacement turned out to be AGPL, I'm searching for an Apache or MIT alternative that can do the same parsing.\\n\\n**[2026-08-15 09:56] Diana**: Any candidates yet?\\n\\n**[2026-08-15 09:58] Charlie**: A couple, but neither one covers everything the old library did. Still unresolved as of today — going to keep looking rather than force a bad fit.\\n\\n**[2026-08-15 10:22] Alice**: Let me know as soon as one of those candidates looks viable — don't want this dragging past the rest of the release work.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 41 slack thread licens parser swap channel cipherdoc thread open 2026 08 11 last activ 2026 08 15 2026 08 11 10 16 evan finish the parser swap the audit flag pull out the problem librari and drop in a replac call that step done 2026 08 11 1018 diana nice turnaround i ll fold it into the re scan 2026 08 11 10 21 charli did you check the new one s licens close or just take the packag list at face valu 2026 08 11 10 22 evan fair question i should have look harder befor wire it in 2026 08 15 09 54 charli follow up on this sinc the replac turn out to be agpl i m search for an apach or mit altern that can do the same pars 2026 08 15 09 56 diana ani candid yet 2026 08 15 09 58 charli a coupl but neither one cover everyth the old librari did still unresolv a of today go to keep look rather than forc a bad fit 2026 08 15 10 22 alic let me know a soon a one of those candid look viabl don t want this drag past the rest of the releas work\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e8f4f0468a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-11-license-parser-swap.md\", \"id\": \"2536eeff413cf064\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.31641865447776, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.14308909211108575, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7208543, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-11-license-parser-swap.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e8f4f0468a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-11-license-parser-swap.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-11-license-parser-swap.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1186, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:04:17\", \"token_count\": 352, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-60\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Async Batch Workers\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-22\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-22 14:21] Bob**: The async processing is looking good. I've integrated the progress callbacks so the GUI can show a real-time percentage.\\n\\n**[2026-08-22 14:30] Diana**: I'm seeing some race conditions when two different users try to process the same file simultaneously. The lock isn't being released correctly.\\n\\n**[2026-08-22 15:00] Bob**: Ah, I see it. I'm using the filename as the key in the lock manager, but not accounting for the user ID.\\n\\n**[2026-08-22 15:02] Charlie**: Why not use the file hash instead? That way even if they have different filenames but it's the same content, we don't process it twice.\\n\\n**[2026-08-22 15:12] Bob**: Good idea. I'll swap out the keys for the SHA-256 hash.\\n\\n**[2026-08-22 15:17] Charlie**: Perfect.\\n\\n**[2026-08-22 15:35] Alice**: @Bob how does this affect the multi-threading work Charlie did?\\n\\n**[2026-08-22 16:56] Bob**: They should play well together. The scheduler distributes the *files* to different workers, and each worker uses Charlie's multi-threaded engine to process the *internal* pages.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 60 slack thread async batch worker channel cipherdoc date 2026 08 22 2026 08 22 14 21 bob the async process is look good i ve integr the progress callback so the gui can show a real time percentag 2026 08 22 14 30 diana i m see some race condit when two differ user tri to process the same file simultan the lock isn t be releas correct 2026 08 22 15 00 bob ah i see it i m use the filenam a the key in the lock manag but not account for the user id 2026 08 22 15 02 charli whi not use the file hash instead that way even if they have differ filenam but it s the same content we don t process it twice 2026 08 22 15 12 bob good idea i ll swap out the key for the sha 256 hash 2026 08 22 15 17 charli perfect 2026 08 22 15 35 alic bob how doe this affect the multi thread work charli did 2026 08 22 16 56 bob they should play well togeth the schedul distribut the file to differ worker and each worker us charli s multi thread engin to process the intern page\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e903a1ae8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-22-async-batch-workers.md\", \"id\": \"238bec23f23e7682\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.31590080313568675, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.17270720447955248, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6500192, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-22-async-batch-workers.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e903a1ae8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-22-async-batch-workers.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-22-async-batch-workers.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1171, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:04:05\", \"token_count\": 352, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}], \"pagination\": {\"page\": 1, \"page_size\": 10, \"total_chunks\": 70, \"total_pages\": 7}, \"query_info\": {\"question\": \"\\\"release blocker\\\" compliance audit September 22 v1.0.0\", \"similarity_threshold\": 0.2, \"vector_weight\": 0.3, \"keyword_search\": false, \"dataset_count\": 1}}"}],"structured_content":null},"error":null,"status":"completed"}}
