n open the task to defin how the engin should resolv overlap redact polici rule 2026 06 16 charli complet complet complet the conflict resolut implement use a union rule for overlap polici 2026 07 17 alic complianc archiv complet record the overlap polici union rule in the complianc pack a durabl evid of the complet conflict resolut rule\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e956a8b88a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-27-Conflict-Resolution.md\", \"id\": \"ea59aa1239fa7470\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3197924904261248, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.14874236918017827, \"vector_similarity\": 0.71890944, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-27-Conflict-Resolution.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e956a8b88a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-27-Conflict-Resolution.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-27-Conflict-Resolution.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1547, \"chunk_count\": 2, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:03:00\", \"token_count\": 586, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-21\\n\\n# Test Note: Air-Gapped Mode Execution\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2021\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-06\\n\\n## Isolated Test Setup\\n\\nTo simulate a strictly offline deployment, we deployed the CLI on a fresh Ubuntu 22.04 VM with the virtual network adapter explicitly disabled (no loopback to host, no NAT). We transferred the application bundle and a 200-document test corpus via a simulated USB mount.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-21\\n\\n# Test Note: Air-Gapped Mode Execution\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2021\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-06\\n\\n## What Worked\\n\\n- The core regex engine and OCR pipeline initialized perfectly without attempting to phone home for license verification or telemetry updates.\\n\\n- The local TPM-based volume encryption successfully mounted the temporary storage drives using the pre-seeded hardware key.\\n\\n- Redaction throughput remained identical to the networked baseline.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-21\\n\\n# Test Note: Air-Gapped Mode Execution\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2021\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-06\\n\\n## Test Limitation\\n\\nThis run built and smoke-tested the harness itself; it did not yet execute a full batch to completion or produce a sign-off. That full run — depending on the already-completed AES-256 encryption pipeline — is the next step and is not reported on here.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 21 test note air gap mode execut owner diana document key doc 2021 last updat 2026 08 06 isol test setup to simul a strict offlin deploy we deploy the cli on a fresh ubuntu 22 04 vm with the virtual network adapt explicit disabl no loopback to host no nat we transfer the applic bundl and a 200 document test corpus via a simul usb mount sourc id src gdoc 21 test note air gap mode execut owner diana document key doc 2021 last updat 2026 08 06 what work the core regex engin and ocr pipelin initi perfect without attempt to phone home for licens verif or telemetri updat the local tpm base volum encrypt success mount the temporari storag drive use the pre seed hardwar key redact throughput remain ident to the network baselin sourc id src gdoc 21 test note air gap mode execut owner diana document key doc 2021 last updat 2026 08 06 test limit this run built and smoke test the har itself it did not yet execut a full batch to complet or produc a sign off that full run depend on the alreadi complet ae 256 encrypt pipelin is the next step and is not report on here\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e9bf73208a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-06-Air-Gapped-Mode-Testing-Review.md\", \"id\": \"978ed7b2e4dfe2fe\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.31404822332679205, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.1033236904668458, \"vector_similarity\": 0.8057388, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-06-Air-Gapped-Mode-Testing-Review.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e9bf73208a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-06-Air-Gapped-Mode-Testing-Review.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-06-Air-Gapped-Mode-Testing-Review.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1063, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:01:25\", \"token_count\": 340, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-46\\n\\n# Design Note: Reproducible Offline Test Harness\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2046\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-06\\n\\n## Why a Harness, Not a One-Off VM\\n\\nAn earlier air-gapped check (see the manual single-VM USB-transfer test) proved the CLI *can* run offline, but it wasn't repeatable — every run required hand-configuring a disconnected machine. T027 calls for a harness that reliably and automatically denies network access on every run, so the offline claim can be re-verified continuously rather than checked once by hand.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-46\\n\\n# Design Note: Reproducible Offline Test Harness\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2046\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-06\\n\\n## Harness Design\\n\\n- Runs the batch CLI inside a dedicated Linux network namespace (`ip netns`) with no interfaces attached except loopback, rather than relying on a physically air-gapped machine.\\n\\n- A wrapper script asserts the namespace has zero routable interfaces before invoking the CLI, and fails the harness run outright — rather than silently proceeding — if any route to the outside world is detected.\\n\\n- Harness output is a pass/fail plus a captured syscall-level network-attempt log, so any code path that *tries* to reach the network, even if it degrades gracefully, is visible for follow-up.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-46\\n\\n# Design Note: Reproducible Offline Test Harness\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2046\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-06\\n\\n## Status\\n\\nDenies network access reliably and repeatably across local test runs. The harness is not yet wired into CI (it currently runs manually), and it validates network denial only — it does not itself certify the full offline batch run for compliance purposes; that sign-off is a separate step.\\n\\n*Status*: Active. Harness reliably enforces network denial; CI integration and any compliance certification are separate, not-yet-complete steps.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 46 design note reproduc offlin test har owner diana document key doc 2046 last updat 2026 08 06 whi a har not a one off vm an earlier air gap check see the manual singl vm usb transfer test prove the cli can run offlin but it wasn t repeat everi run requir hand configur a disconnect machin t027 call for a har that reliabl and automat deni network access on everi run so the offlin claim can be re verifi continu rather than check onc by hand sourc id src gdoc 46 design note reproduc offlin test har owner diana document key doc 2046 last updat 2026 08 06 har design run the batch cli insid a dedic linux network namespac ip netn with no interfac attach except loopback rather than reli on a physic air gap machin a wrapper script assert the namespac ha zero routabl interfac befor invok the cli and fail the har run outright rather than silent proceed if ani rout to the outsid world is detect har output is a pas fail plus a captur syscal level network attempt log so ani code path that tri to reach the network even if it degrad grace is visibl for follow up sourc id src gdoc 46 design note reproduc offlin test har owner diana document key doc 2046 last updat 2026 08 06 status deni network access reliabl and repeat across local test run the har is not yet wire into ci it current run manual and it valid network denial onli it doe not itself certifi the full offlin batch run for complianc purpos that sign off is a separ step status activ har reliabl enforc network denial ci integr and ani complianc certif are separ not yet complet step\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e9d8406c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-06-Air-Gapped-Mode-Harness-Design.md\", \"id\": \"26a2e97fa1bb8b9c\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.30897884674148074, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.10978142105925821, \"vector_similarity\": 0.77377284, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-06-Air-Gapped-Mode-Harness-Design.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e9d8406c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-06-Air-Gapped-Mode-Harness-Design.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-06-Air-Gapped-Mode-Harness-Design.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1618, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:01:07\", \"token_count\": 465, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"# ClickUp Task: CIPH-29\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-29\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-29\\n\\n**Title**: Offline auth with key rotation for air-gapped installs\\n\\n**Status**: Blocked\\n\\n**Assignee**: Diana\\n\\n**Priority**: High\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-08-01\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nProvide offline-mode authentication for air-gapped deployments, including a key-rotation flow that doesn't assume an always-on network. Testing against a local auth mock showed that key rotation cannot complete without network access in an air-gapped setting, and the task remains blocked with no resolution yet.\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-29\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-29\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-29\\n\\n**Title**: Offline auth with key rotation for air-gapped installs\\n\\n**Status**: Blocked\\n\\n**Assignee**: Diana\\n\\n**Priority**: High\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-08-01\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- Authentication works fully offline for air-gapped deployment scenarios.\\n\\n- Key-rotation flow completes without requiring network access.\\n\\n- Blocking issue (rotation dependent on network) is resolved before the task can close.\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-29\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-29\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-29\\n\\n**Title**: Offline auth with key rotation for air-gapped installs\\n\\n**Status**: Blocked\\n\\n**Assignee**: Diana\\n\\n**Priority**: High\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-08-01\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nProvide offline-mode authentication for air-gapped deployments, including a key-rotation flow that doesn't assume an always-on network. Testing against a local auth mock showed that key rotation cannot complete without network access in an air-gapped setting, and the task remains blocked with no resolution yet.\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-29\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-29\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-29\\n\\n**Title**: Offline auth with key rotation for air-gapped installs\\n\\n**Status**: Blocked\\n\\n**Assignee**: Diana\\n\\n**Priority**: High\\n\\n**Date Created**: 20