37e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-04-offline-auth-mock-block.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-04-offline-auth-mock-block.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1092, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:04:54\", \"token_count\": 340, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"# ClickUp Task: CIPH-31\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-31\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-31\\n\\n**Title**: Encrypt redacted outputs with AES-256 at rest\\n\\n**Status**: Completed\\n\\n**Assignee**: Bob\\n\\n**Priority**: High\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-08-01\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nAdd local at-rest encryption for redacted outputs using AES-256, suitable for the offline runtime. Security signed off on the AES-256 pipeline once it could rely on the completed fail-closed deletion behavior.\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-31\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-31\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-31\\n\\n**Title**: Encrypt redacted outputs with AES-256 at rest\\n\\n**Status**: Completed\\n\\n**Assignee**: Bob\\n\\n**Priority**: High\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-08-01\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- Redacted outputs are encrypted at rest using AES-256.\\n\\n- Encryption pipeline works within the offline/local runtime constraints.\\n\\n- Crypto sign-off is obtained, contingent on the completed fail-closed deletion behavior it depends on.\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-31\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-31\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-31\\n\\n**Title**: Encrypt redacted outputs with AES-256 at rest\\n\\n**Status**: Completed\\n\\n**Assignee**: Bob\\n\\n**Priority**: High\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-08-01\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nAdd local at-rest encryption for redacted outputs using AES-256, suitable for the offline runtime. Security signed off on the AES-256 pipeline once it could rely on the completed fail-closed deletion behavior.\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-31\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-31\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-31\\n\\n**Title**: Encrypt redacted outputs with AES-256 at rest\\n\\n**Status**: Completed\\n\\n**Assignee**: Bob\\n\\n**Priority**: High\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-08-01\\n\\n## Activity History\\n\\n- **2026-08-01**: Alice - Task Create (Open)\\n\\n - *Opened the task because redacted outputs need local at-rest encryption.*\\n\\n- **2026-08-07**: Diana - Crypto Sign-off (Completed)\\n\\n - *Signed off on the AES-256 encryption pipeline now that it could rely on the completed fail-closed deletion behavior.*\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"clickup task ciph 31 sourc id src cu ciph 31 task id ciph 31 titl encrypt redact output with ae 256 at rest status complet assigne bob prioriti high date creat 2026 0801 descript add local at rest encrypt for redact output use ae 256 suitabl for the offlin runtim secur sign off on the ae 256 pipelin onc it could reli on the complet fail close delet behavior clickup task ciph 31 sourc id src cu ciph 31 task id ciph 31 titl encrypt redact output with ae 256 at rest status complet assigne bob prioriti high date creat 2026 0801 accept criterion redact output are encrypt at rest use ae 256 encrypt pipelin work within the offlin local runtim constraint crypto sign off is obtain conting on the complet fail close delet behavior it depend on clickup task ciph 31 sourc id src cu ciph 31 task id ciph 31 titl encrypt redact output with ae 256 at rest status complet assigne bob prioriti high date creat 2026 0801 descript add local at rest encrypt for redact output use ae 256 suitabl for the offlin runtim secur sign off on the ae 256 pipelin onc it could reli on the complet fail close delet behavior clickup task ciph 31 sourc id src cu ciph 31 task id ciph 31 titl encrypt redact output with ae 256 at rest status complet assigne bob prioriti high date creat 2026 0801 activ histori 2026 0801 alic task creat open open the task becaus redact output need local at rest encrypt 2026 08 07 diana crypto sign off complet sign off on the ae 256 encrypt pipelin now that it could reli on the complet fail close delet behavior\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e988799c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-31-Local-Encryption-at-Rest.md\", \"id\": \"a396b89ca9489cae\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.29196606691210336, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.09686595987443342, \"vector_similarity\": 0.74719965, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-31-Local-Encryption-at-Rest.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e988799c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-31-Local-Encryption-at-Rest.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-31-Local-Encryption-at-Rest.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1024, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:02:13\", \"token_count\": 524, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-35\\n\\n# Crypto Sign-off: AES-256 At-Rest Encryption Pipeline\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2035\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-07\\n\\n## Sign-off Basis\\n\\nSecurity sign-off on the AES-256 at-rest pipeline was withheld until the fail-closed deletion behavior for interrupted redaction runs (T015) was confirmed Completed — an unencrypted partial output left on disk after a crash would have undermined the encryption guarantee entirely. With that dependency cleared, the sign-off proceeded against the pipeline as implemented.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-35\\n\\n# Crypto Sign-off: AES-256 At-Rest Encryption Pipeline\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2035\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-07\\n\\n## What Was Reviewed\\n\\n- AES-256-GCM authenticated encryption applied to every redacted output file before it is written to its final location.\\n\\n- Key handling confined to process memory; no plaintext key material written to disk or logs.\\n\\n- Confirmed the pipeline degrades safely (refuses to write plaintext) if key material is unavailable, consistent with the fail-closed contract from T015.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-35\\n\\n# Crypto Sign-off: AES-256 At-Rest Encryption Pipeline\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2035\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-07\\n\\n## Follow-up Noted at Sign-off\\n\\nOn machines without a hardware TPM, the volume key is still derived from a user passphrase via PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA256 at 100k iterations. This is not a blocker for the AES-256 pipeline sign-off itself, but Diana flagged it as a hardening follow-up: moving to Argon2id would meaningfully raise the cost of offline brute-force against weak passphrases on non-TPM hardware.\\n\\n*Status*: AES-256 at-rest pipeline signed off as Completed. Passphrase-derived key hardening (Argon2id) tracked separately as a pre-v1.0 hardening item, not a sign-off condition.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 35 crypto sign off ae 256 at rest encrypt pipelin owner diana document key doc 2035 last updat 2026 08 07 sign off basi secur sign off on the ae 256 at rest pipelin wa withheld until the fail close delet behavior for interrupt redact run t015 wa confirm complet an unencrypt partial output left on disk after a crash would have undermin the encrypt guarante entir with that depend clear the sign off proceed against the pipelin a implement sourc id src gdoc 35 crypto sign off ae 256 at rest encrypt pipelin owner diana document key doc 2035 last updat 2026 08 07 what wa review ae 256 gcm authent encrypt appli to everi redact output file befor it is written to it final locat key handl confin to process memori no plaintext key materi written to disk or log confirm the pipelin degrad safe refus to write plaintext if key materi is unavail consist with the fail close contract from t015 sourc id src gdoc 35 crypto sign off ae 256 at rest encrypt pipelin owner diana document key doc 2035 last updat 2026 08 07 follow up note at sign off on machin without a hardwar tpm the volum key is still deriv from a user passphras via pbkdf2 hmac sha256 at 100k iter this is not a blocker for the ae 256 pipelin sign off itself but diana flag it a a harden follow up move to argon2id would meaning rais the cost of offlin brute forc against weak passphras on non tpm hardwar status ae 256 at rest pipelin sign off a complet passphras deriv key harden argon2id track separ a a pre v1 0 harden item not a sign off condit\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e99eb05e8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-07-Local-Encryption-at-Rest-Security-Evaluation.md\", \"id\": \"3d30fbd4bb571642\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.290156099082726, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.08395049868960859, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7713025, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-07-Local-Encryption-at-Rest-Security-Evaluation.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e99eb05e8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-07-Local-Encryption-at-Rest-Security-Evaluation.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-07-Local-Encryption-at-Rest-Security-Evaluation.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1518, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:01:57\", \"token_count\": 466, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}],