\n\\nThe produced build artifact is unsigned, which triggers a SmartScreen warning and Defender flagging the binary as untrusted.\\n\\n- **Impact**: Site IT policies commonly block execution of unsigned/SmartScreen-flagged binaries outright, which would prevent installation on target deployment workstations without a manual security-policy override.\\n\\n- **Root Cause**: No code-signing certificate has been procured or configured in the Windows build pipeline yet.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-39\\n\\n# Compatibility Audit: Windows Build Signing Gap\\n\\n**Owner**: Evan\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2039\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-02\\n\\n## Path to Resolution\\n\\nProcuring a code-signing certificate and wiring signing into the release build step is the only remaining item before this clears the T029 Windows compatibility gate — and, by extension, the T011 release checklist, which is holding on this exact signing gap alongside the T005 image slim-down.\\n\\n*Audit Status*: Active. Build produces successfully; signing certificate procurement is the sole open blocker.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 39 compat audit window build sign gap owner evan document key doc 2039 last updat 2026 09 02 background path fix clear packag backslash path handl defect that previous broke window build were fix on 2026 08 10 and a window build artifact wa success produc by 2026 08 12 packag itself is no longer the blocker sourc id src gdoc 39 compat audit window build sign gap owner evan document key doc 2039 last updat 2026 09 02 current blocker miss code sign certif the produc build artifact is unsign which trigger a smartscreen warn and defend flag the binari a untrust impact site it polici common block execut of unsign smartscreen flag binari outright which would prevent instal on target deploy workstat without a manual secur polici overrid root caus no code sign certif ha been procur or configur in the window build pipelin yet sourc id src gdoc 39 compat audit window build sign gap owner evan document key doc 2039 last updat 2026 09 02 path to resolut procur a code sign certif and wire sign into the releas build step is the onli remain item befor this clear the t029 window compat gate and by extens the t011 releas checklist which is hold on this exact sign gap alongsid the t005 imag slim down audit status activ build produc success sign certif procur is the sole open blocker\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e9aa652a8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-02-Windows-Compatibility-Audit-Report.md\", \"id\": \"7d9dbdfb5b6d7c2f\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.25282143065238594, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.07282448664626562, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6728143, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-02-Windows-Compatibility-Audit-Report.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e9aa652a8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-02-Windows-Compatibility-Audit-Report.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-02-Windows-Compatibility-Audit-Report.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1340, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:01:48\", \"token_count\": 387, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-09\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Security Patch - CORS Issue\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Thread opened**: 2026-07-10\\n\\n**Last activity**: 2026-07-15\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-07-10 14:20] Diana**: @Bob, I just ran a security scan on the API. We've got a wide-open CORS policy. `Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *` is a no-go for this project.\\n\\n**[2026-07-10 14:23] Bob**: Oops, that was left over from local testing on the scaffold. I'll tighten it up now.\\n\\n**[2026-07-10 14:43] Bob**: Applying the CORS patch. It now only allows requests from the defined `ALLOWED_ORIGINS` in the environment config.\\n\\n**[2026-07-10 14:50] Diana**: Scan is coming back clean now.\\n\\n**[2026-07-10 14:52] Bob**: Thanks for the catch, Diana. I've added a lint check to prevent `*` from being committed in the future.\\n\\n**[2026-07-10 15:45] Alice**: Good catch. Let's make sure we don't have any other dev-only flags leaking into the main branch.\\n\\n**[2026-07-15 09:54] Diana**: Re-ran the CVE and CORS scans ahead of the release evidence pack — patch is still holding, no regressions since Bob's fix.\\n\\n**[2026-07-15 09:55] Bob**: Good. I'll note that in the security patch record.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 09 slack thread secur patch cor issu channel cipherdoc thread open 2026 07 10 last activ 2026 07 15 2026 07 10 14 20 diana bob i just ran a secur scan on the api we ve got a wide open cor polici access control allow origin is a no go for this project 2026 07 10 14 23 bob oop that wa left over from local test on the scaffold i ll tighten it up now 2026 07 10 14 43 bob appli the cor patch it now onli allow request from the defin allow _ origin in the environ config 2026 07 10 14 50 diana scan is come back clean now 2026 07 10 14 52 bob thank for the catch diana i ve ad a lint check to prevent from be commit in the futur 2026 07 1015 45 alic good catch let s make sure we don t have ani other dev onli flag leak into the main branch 2026 07 15 09 54 diana re ran the cve and cor scan ahead of the releas evid pack patch is still hold no regress sinc bob s fix 2026 07 15 09 55 bob good i ll note that in the secur patch record\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e92a731a8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communicati